INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 1, 1, 'And so on that cold and wintry November morning, the boy Kolya Krasotkin was sitting at home.', 'The passage begins by setting the scene: it is a cold, wintry November morning, and the main character, a boy named Kolya Krasotkin, is at his residence.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 2, 1, 'It was Sunday, and there was no school.', 'The specific day is noted as Sunday, meaning Kolya had the day off from school.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 3, 1, 'But the clock had just struck eleven and he absolutely had to go out “on very important business,” and yet there he was, left alone in the whole house and decidedly in harge of it, because it so happened that all of its elder inhabitants were away, owing to some urgent and singular circumstance.', 'Although it was 11:00 AM and he needed to depart for a crucial, secret engagement, Kolya remained at home because he was the sole person left in charge of the entire house, as the adults had all gone out due to an unexpected and strange situation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 4, 2, 'There was only one other apartment in the widow Krasotkin’s house, two little rooms across the hall from the widow’s apartment, which she rented out, and which were occupied by a doctor’s wife with two small children.', 'The house, owned by Kolya’s mother, the widow Krasotkin, contained a single rental unit of two small rooms across the hall, which were currently occupied by a doctor\'s wife and her two young children.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 5, 2, 'This doctor’s wife was the same age as Anna Fyodorovna, and a great friend of hers, while the doctor himself had gone off somewhere about a year before, first to Orenburg, then to Tashkent, and nothing had been heard of him for the past six months, so that had it not been for the friendship of Mrs. Krasotkin, which somewhat softened the grief of the doctor’s abandoned wife, she would decidedly have drowned herself in the tears of that grief.', 'The doctor\'s wife was a close friend and peer of Mrs. Krasotkin Anna Fyodorovna; her husband had vanished a year ago and been unheard from for six months, meaning that Mrs. Krasotkin\'s comforting friendship was the only thing preventing the abandoned wife from utter despair.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 6, 3, 'And now it so happened, as if to crown all the adversities of fate, that Katerina, the doctor’s wife’s only maid, suddenly, and quite unexpectedly for her mistress, announced to her that very night, on Saturday, that she intended to give birth to a baby the next morning.', 'Adding to the woman’s misfortunes, her only maid, Katerina, abruptly and without warning informed her on Saturday night that she was going into labor and would give birth the next day.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 7, 3, 'How it happened that no one had noticed it before struck everyone as almost miraculous.', 'The fact that Katerina’s pregnancy had gone completely unnoticed until the last moment seemed almost supernatural to all involved.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 8, 3, 'The amazed doctor’s wife judged it best, while there was still time, to take Katerina to an establishment kept by a midwife in our town, suitable for such occasions.', 'The shocked doctor\'s wife immediately decided it was wisest to transport Katerina to a local midwife’s birthing establishment while there was still an opportunity.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 9, 3, 'Since she highly valued her maid, she put her plan into action at once, took her there, and moreover stayed there with her.', 'Because she greatly cared for Katerina, the mistress executed the plan immediately, taking the maid and staying by her side.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 10, 3, 'Later, in the morning, for some reason there was need for all the friendly participation and help of Mrs. Krasotkin herself, who on such an occasion could ask someone for something and wield a certain influence.', 'Later that morning, Mrs. Krasotkin’s friendly assistance and influence were required, likely because she was capable of making requests or exerting authority in that type of situation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 11, 3, 'Thus both ladies were absent, and as for Mrs. Krasotkin’s own maid, Agafya, she had gone to the market, and thus Kolya found himself for a time the keeper and guardian of the “squirts”—that is, the doctor’s wife’s little boy and girl, who were left all alone.', 'As a result of these events, both Mrs. Krasotkin and the doctor\'s wife were gone, and because Mrs. Krasotkin’s maid, Agafya, was at the market, Kolya was left temporarily in charge of the doctor\'s wife\'s children, whom he nicknamed the \"squirts.\"', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 12, 4, 'Kolya was not afraid of guarding the house; besides he had Perezvon, who was ordered to lie down and “stay” under the bench in the front hall, and, precisely for that reason, every time Kolya, who kept pacing the rooms, came out to the hall, he shook his head and gave two firm and ingratiating thumps on the floor with his tail, but, alas, the summoning whistle did not come.', 'Kolya felt secure in his role guarding the house, especially since his dog, Perezvon, was on a strict \"stay\" command under the hall bench, and though the dog would shake his head and thump his tail eagerly whenever Kolya passed by while pacing, Kolya refused to give the whistle that would release him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 13, 4, 'Kolya would give the miserable dog a severe look, and again the dog would obediently freeze.', 'If the dog showed too much enthusiasm, Kolya would give him a stern glance, causing the dog to immediately stop and remain still again.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 14, 4, 'But if anything troubled Kolya, it was the “squirts.”', 'Kolya’s primary source of worry was not the house, but the children he was responsible for.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 15, 4, 'He naturally looked with the deepest contempt upon the unexpected adventure with Katerina, but the orphaned squirts he loved very much, and he had already brought them some children’s book.', 'He completely dismissed the odd circumstances surrounding Katerina’s labor, but he genuinely cared for the children and had already given them a book to keep them occupied.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 16, 5, 'The older of the two, the girl Nastya, was eight and knew how to read, and the younger squirt, the seven-year-old boy, Kostya, liked it very much when Nastya read to him.', 'The eight-year-old girl, Nastya, was the elder child and was able to read, and the seven-year-old boy, Kostya, thoroughly enjoyed listening to his sister read aloud.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 17, 5, 'Naturally, Krasotkin knew more interesting ways of entertaining them—for instance, by standing them side by side and playing soldiers, or hiding all over the house.', 'Kolya usually had more exciting methods of amusement, such as having them play soldiers or hide-and-seek throughout the residence.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 18, 5, 'He had done it more than once before and did not consider it beneath him, so that the rumor had even spread in his class that Krasotkin played “horses” at home with his little tenants, prancing and tossing his head like an outrunner, but Krasotkin proudly parried the accusation, putting forward the argument that “in our day” it would indeed be disgraceful to play “horses” with one’s peers, with thirteen-year-olds, but that he did so with the “squirts” because he loved them, and no one should dare call him to account for his feelings.', 'Kolya had engaged in such games often and was not embarrassed by them; even when rumors reached his classmates that he played \"horses\" with the younger tenants, he countered by proudly asserting that while it would be shameful to play with thirteen-year-old friends, he did it for the younger children out of love, and no one had the right to judge his emotional motives.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 19, 5, 'And how the two “squirts” adored him!', 'The two children clearly reciprocated his affection and idolized him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 20, 5, 'But this was no time for games.', 'However, at this moment, engaging in games was impossible.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 21, 5, 'He was faced with some very important business of his own, which somehow even appeared almost mysterious, and meanwhile time was passing, and Agafya, with whom he could have left the children, still refused to come back from the market.', 'Kolya had his own urgent and seemingly secret task to attend to, and as time was running out, Agafya, the maid he needed to relieve him, had not yet returned from the market.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 22, 5, 'He had already gone across the hall several times, opened the door to the other apartment, and looked in anxiously at the “squirts,” who, on his orders, were sitting there with a book, and, each time he opened the door, gave him big, silent smiles, expecting him to come in and do something wonderful and amusing.', 'He had repeatedly crossed the hall to check on the children in their apartment, where they were sitting with a book as instructed, and each time they would look up with quiet, wide smiles, hoping he would enter to entertain them.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 23, 5, 'But Kolya was troubled in his soul and would not go in.', 'Kolya was internally distressed by his situation and refrained from entering their room.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 24, 5, 'Finally it struck eleven and he decided firmly and ultimately that if in ten minutes that “cursed” Agafya had not come back, he would leave without waiting for her, of course making the “squirts” give their word that they would not be scared without him, would not get into mischief, and would not cry from fear.', 'Once the clock struck eleven, he made a definitive decision: if the \"cursed\" Agafya was not back in ten minutes, he would depart without her, but first, he would extract a promise from the children not to be afraid, get into trouble, or cry while he was gone.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 25, 6, 'With that thought in mind, he put on his padded winter coat with some kind of sealskin collar, slung his bag over his shoulder, and, despite his mother’s oft-repeated pleadings that he not go out “in such cold” without his galoshes, merely glanced at them in disdain, passing through the hall, and went out in just his boots.', 'Preparing to act on his decision, he donned his warm coat and bag, deliberately ignoring his mother’s frequent warnings about the cold and his need for galoshes, looking at them with contempt as he walked through the hall, wearing only his boots.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 26, 6, 'Perezvon, as soon as he saw him with his coat on, began thumping the floor still harder with his tail, nervously twitching all over, and even uttered a pitiful howl, but Kolya, seeing such passionate yearning in his dog, decided it was bad discipline, and kept him longer, though just a moment longer, under the bench, and only as he was opening the door to the hall did he suddenly whistle for him.', 'Upon seeing Kolya dressed for going out, Perezvon\'s excitement intensified, causing him to thump his tail harder, twitch nervously, and let out a sad whimper; Kolya viewed this eagerness as poor discipline, kept him under the bench for one last moment, and only released him with a sudden whistle as he opened the door to the hall.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 27, 6, 'The dog jumped up madly and began leaping ecstatically in front of him.', 'The moment he was released, the dog jumped up with wild joy and began jumping excitedly around Kolya.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 28, 6, 'Kolya crossed the hall and opened the “squirts’ “ door.', 'Kolya walked across the hall and opened the door to the children’s apartment.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 29, 6, 'They were both still sitting at the table, not reading now, but arguing heatedly about something.', 'He saw that both children were still seated at the table, but instead of reading, they were engaged in an intense argument.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 30, 6, 'The children often argued with each other about various provocative matters of life, and Nastya, being older, always had the upper hand; and Kostya, if he did not agree with her, almost always went to appeal to Kolya Krasotkin, and whatever he decided remained the ultimate verdict for all sides.', 'The two children frequently debated controversial subjects, with the older Nastya usually dominating the discussion; if Kostya disagreed, he would usually seek Kolya Krasotkin\'s judgment, which was considered final by everyone.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 31, 6, 'This time the argument between the “squirts” somewhat interested Krasotkin, and he stopped in the doorway to listen.', 'Kolya found the children\'s current argument intriguing, prompting him to stop in the doorway and eavesdrop.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 32, 6, 'The children saw he was listening and carried on their dispute with even greater enthusiasm.', 'Noticing Kolya\'s attention, the children became even more eager in their debate.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 33, 7, '“I’ll never, ever believe,” Nastya ardently prattled, “that midwives find little babies in the vegetable garden, between the cabbage rows.', 'Nastya passionately declared that she could not believe the common story that babies are found by midwives in the vegetable garden, specifically between cabbage rows.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 34, 7, 'It’s winter now and there aren’t any cabbage rows, and the midwife couldn’t have brought Katerina a baby girl.”', 'She logically pointed out that since it was winter and there were no cabbage rows, the midwife could not have used that method to bring Katerina a baby girl.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 35, 8, '“Whe-ew!” Kolya whistled to himself.', 'Kolya reacted silently with a sound of surprise or disbelief at the topic of their discussion.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 36, 9, '“Or maybe it’s like this: they do bring them from somewhere, but only when people get married.”', 'Kostya proposed a different idea: that babies are brought from an unknown source, but only in the case of married people.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 37, 9, 'Kostya stared at Nastya, listened gravely, and pondered.', 'He looked seriously at Nastya, absorbed what was said, and contemplated the situation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 38, 10, '“Nastya, what a fool you are,” he said at last, firmly and without excitement.', 'Kostya eventually called Nastya a fool, stating it calmly and decisively.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 39, 10, '“Where could Katerina get a baby if she’s not married?”', 'He rationally challenged her, asking how Katerina, who was unmarried, could possibly obtain a baby.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 40, 11, 'Nastya grew terribly excited.', 'Nastya became extremely agitated by his question.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 41, 11, '“You don’t understand anything,” she cut him short irritably.', 'She quickly and impatiently interrupted him, saying he lacked understanding.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 42, 11, '“Maybe she had a husband, but he’s in prison now, so she went and had a baby.”', 'She offered an alternative explanation: Katerina might have a husband who is currently imprisoned, which is why she is having a baby.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 43, 12, '“But is her husband in prison?” the staid Kostya inquired gravely.', 'The composed Kostya seriously and formally asked for confirmation about the husband’s imprisonment.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 44, 13, '“Or else,” Nastya swiftly interrupted, completely abandoning and forgetting her first hypothesis, “she hasn’t got a husband, you’re right about that, but she wants to get married, so she started thinking how to get married, and she kept thinking and thinking, and she thought so much that now she got a baby instead.”', 'Nastya quickly introduced a new, completely different theory, agreeing that Katerina had no husband, but suggesting that her intense and continuous thoughts about getting married somehow resulted in her having a baby.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 45, 14, '“Well, maybe,” agreed the utterly defeated Kostya, “but you didn’t say that before, so how could I know?”', 'Kostya, completely overwhelmed by her argument, conceded the point but defended himself by saying he couldn\'t have known her new theory since she hadn\'t mentioned it earlier.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 46, 15, '“Well, kids,” said Kolya, taking a step into the room, “you’re dangerous people, I see!”', 'Taking a step into the room, Kolya spoke to the children, jokingly calling them \"dangerous people\" due to their bold conversation topic.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 47, 16, '“And Perezvon, too?” Kostya grinned, and began snapping his fingers and calling Perezvon.', 'Kostya smiled and asked if the dog Perezvon was also dangerous, attempting to summon the dog by snapping his fingers.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 48, 17, '“I’m in trouble, squirts,” Krasotkin began importantly, “and you’ve got to help me: of course Agafya must have broken her leg, since she’s not back yet, that’s signed and sealed, but I have to leave.', 'Kolya started speaking with a serious tone, informing the children he was in a difficult position and needed their help, declaring that Agafya\'s lateness definitely meant she had broken her leg, but he still had to depart.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 49, 17, 'Will you let me go or not?”', 'He asked them for their consent to his leaving.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 50, 18, 'The children worriedly exchanged looks, their grinning faces showed signs of anxiety.', 'The children looked at each other with concern, their smiles replaced by signs of worry.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 51, 18, 'However, they still did not quite understand what was wanted of them.', 'Despite their concern, they did not fully grasp the precise nature of the commitment Kolya was requesting.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 52, 19, '“You won’t get into mischief while I’m gone?', 'Kolya asked them to promise not to misbehave in his absence.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 53, 19, 'You won’t climb on the cupboard and break your leg?', 'He asked them not to endanger themselves by doing things like climbing the furniture.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 54, 19, 'You won’t cry from fear if you’re left alone?”', 'He asked for their assurance that they would not cry out of fear from being left without him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 55, 20, 'Terrible grief showed on the children’s faces.', 'The possibility of being left alone and making these promises caused the children’s faces to show great sadness.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 56, 21, '“And to make up for it I’ll show you a little something—it’s a little brass cannon that shoots with real powder.”', 'To console them for his departure, Kolya offered to show them a small brass cannon that actually fires with gunpowder.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 57, 22, 'The children’s faces brightened at once.', 'The mention of the cannon instantly cheered up the children.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 58, 22, '“Show us the little cannon,” Kostya said, beaming all over.', 'Kostya, now radiant with happiness, eagerly requested to see the small cannon.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 59, 23, 'Krasotkin thrust his hand into his bag, pulled out a little bronze cannon, and placed it on the table.', 'Kolya reached into his bag, produced the small bronze cannon, and set it down on the table.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 60, 23, '“‘Show us, show us! ‘ Look, it has little wheels,” he drove the toy along the table, “and it can shoot.', 'Mimicking their excitement, he pointed out the small wheels on the cannon, rolled it along the table, and confirmed its firing capability.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 61, 23, 'Load it with small shot and it shoots.”', 'He explained that the cannon would fire when loaded with small metal pellets.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 62, 24, '“And can it kill somebody?”', 'One of the children inquired if the cannon was powerful enough to kill a person.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 63, 25, '“It can kill everybody, you just have to aim it,” and Krasotkin explained how to put in the powder and roll in the shot, showed the little hole for the primer, and explained to them that there was such a thing as recoil.', 'Kolya dramatically claimed it could kill anyone if aimed properly, and proceeded to demonstrate how to load the gunpowder and shot, pointed out the hole for the primer, and explained the concept of a backward jolt called recoil.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 64, 25, 'The children listened with terrible curiosity.', 'The children listened to his explanation with intense fascination.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 65, 25, 'What particularly struck their imagination was that there was such a thing as recoil.', 'The idea of the cannon recoiling after a shot was the detail that most impressed the children.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 66, 26, '“And have you got some powder?” Nastya inquired.', 'Nastya asked if Kolya actually possessed the gunpowder needed for the cannon.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 67, 27, '“I have.”', 'Kolya confirmed that he had the powder.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 68, 28, '“Show us the powder, too,” she whined with an imploring smile.', 'Nastya, with a pleading smile, begged him to let them see the gunpowder as well.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 69, 29, 'Krasotkin again went into his bag, and took out of it a small bottle, which indeed contained some real powder, and a folded paper, which turned out to have a few pellets of shot in it.', 'Kolya reached into his bag a second time and pulled out a small bottle containing real powder and a folded piece of paper containing several pellets of shot.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 70, 29, 'He even opened the bottle and poured a little powder out in his palm.', 'He proceeded to open the bottle and pour a small quantity of the powder into his hand.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 71, 29, '“So long as there’s no fire around, or it would explode and kill us all,” Krasotkin warned, for the sake of effect.', 'For dramatic impact, Kolya issued a caution that the powder could explode and kill everyone if there was any fire nearby.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 72, 29, 'The children gazed at the powder with an awestruck fear, which only increased their pleasure.', 'The children looked at the powder with a mix of reverence and terror, which surprisingly intensified their enjoyment of the moment.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 73, 29, 'But Kostya liked the shot better.', 'Kostya, however, was more drawn to the metal pellets than the powder.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 74, 30, '“Does shot burn?” he inquired.', 'Kostya asked if the metal shot was flammable.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 75, 31, '“Shot does not burn.”', 'Kolya replied that the shot would not burn.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 76, 32, '“Give me some shot,” he said in a pleading voice.', 'Kostya used a begging tone to ask for some of the shot.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 77, 33, '“I’ll give you a little, here, take it, only don’t show it to your mother before I come back, or she may think it’s powder, and she’ll die of fear and give you a whipping.”', 'Kolya gave him a small amount but warned him to hide it from his mother until Kolya returned, implying she might mistake it for powder, panic, and punish him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 78, 33, '“Mama never beats us,” Nastya observed at once.', 'Nastya immediately corrected him by stating that their mother never hit them.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 79, 33, '“I know, I just said it for the beauty of the style.”', 'Kolya conceded that he knew this, claiming he had said it merely for the rhetorical effect.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 80, 33, '“And you should never deceive your mama, except this once—till I come back.”', 'He instructed them never to lie to their mother, with the single exception of hiding the shot until he returned.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 81, 33, '“Well, squirts, can I go or not?', 'He repeated his question, asking for their permission to leave.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 82, 33, 'Are you going to cry from fear without me?”', 'He asked again if they would become frightened and cry if he left.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 83, 34, '“We w-will c-cry,” Kostya whined, already preparing to cry.', 'Kostya, on the verge of tears, admitted they would cry.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 84, 34, '“We will, we really will cry!” Nastya added in a frightened patter.', 'Nastya also quickly and anxiously confirmed that they definitely would cry.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 85, 35, '“Oh, children, children, how perilous are your years.278', 'Kolya sighed, commenting on the dangerous vulnerability of their young age.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 86, 35, 'So, there’s nothing to be done, chicks, I’ll have to stay with you I don’t know how long.', 'He concluded that he was left with no choice but to remain with them for an indeterminate period.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 87, 35, 'And the time, the time, oof!”', 'He expressed his frustration and regret over the valuable time he was losing.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 88, 36, '“Tell Perezvon to play dead,” Kostya asked.', 'Kostya asked Kolya to command Perezvon to perform his trick of playing dead.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 89, 37, '“Well, nothing to be done, I’ll have to resort to Perezvon.', 'Kolya reluctantly agreed that using the dog\'s tricks was his only recourse.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 90, 37, 'Ici, Perezvon!”', 'He called the dog using the French command, \"Here, Perezvon!\"', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 91, 37, 'And Kolya began giving orders to the dog, and he began doing all his tricks.', 'Kolya started issuing commands, and the dog began performing its various tricks.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 92, 37, 'He was a shaggy dog, the size of any ordinary mongrel, with a sort of blue gray coat.', 'The dog is described as a shaggy, medium-sized mixed-breed with a blue-gray coat.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 93, 37, 'He was blind in his right eye, and his left ear for some reason had a nick in it.', 'Further details are given: he was blind in his right eye and had a notch in his left ear.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 94, 37, 'He squealed and jumped, stood and walked on his hind legs, threw himself on his back with all four legs in the air and lay motionless as if dead.', 'The dog performed its repertoire, which included whimpering, leaping, walking bipedally, and finally lying perfectly still on his back with all four legs raised, pretending to be deceased.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 95, 37, 'During this last trick the door opened and Agafya, Mrs. Krasotkin’s fat maid, a pockmarked woman of about forty, appeared on the threshold, returning from the market with a paper bag full of groceries in her hand.', 'While the dog was playing dead, Mrs. Krasotkin’s maid, Agafya, a plump, pockmarked woman of about forty, appeared in the doorway, having returned from the market with a bag of groceries.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 96, 37, 'She stood with the bag perched on her left hand and began watching the dog.', 'Agafya paused in the doorway, balancing the grocery bag on her hand, and watched the dog perform.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 97, 37, 'Kolya, however eagerly he had been waiting for Agafya, did not interrupt the performance, and having kept Perezvon dead for a certain length of time, finally whistled: the dog jumped up and began leaping for joy at having fulfilled his duty.', 'Despite how desperately Kolya had been waiting for her, he let the dog finish the \"dead\" trick for the required time before whistling, whereupon Perezvon immediately jumped up and bounded happily, having completed his command.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 98, 38, '“Some dog that is!” Agafya said didactically.', 'Agafya commented on the dog’s skill with a tone of instruction or judgment.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 99, 39, '“Why are you late, female sex?” Krasotkin asked sternly.', 'Kolya sternly asked the maid why she, whom he referred to as \"female sex,\" was late.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 100, 39, '“Female sex yourself, pipsqueak.”', 'Agafya responded by using Kolya’s term against him and insulting him by calling him a \"pipsqueak.\"', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 101, 40, '“Pipsqueak?”', 'Kolya questioned her use of the word \"pipsqueak.\"', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 102, 41, '“Yes, pipsqueak.', 'Agafya affirmed that she had called him a pipsqueak.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 103, 41, 'What’s it to you if I’m late?', 'She defensively asked why his business was affected by her tardiness.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 104, 41, 'If I’m late I must have had good reason,” Agafya muttered, as she started bustling about the stove, not at all in a displeased or angry voice, but, on the contrary, sounding very pleased, as if she were glad of the chance to exchange quips with her cheerful young master.', 'Agafya muttered that her lateness was surely justified as she began moving around the stove, speaking not with irritation but with apparent enjoyment, suggesting she welcomed the opportunity for a playful exchange with the young master.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 105, 42, '“Listen, you frivolous old woman,” Krasotkin began, rising from the sofa, “will you swear to me by all that’s holy in this world, and something else besides, that you will keep a constant eye on the squirts in my absence?', 'Kolya stood up and addressed her with an air of authority, demanding that the \"frivolous old woman\" swear by everything sacred, and more, that she would continuously supervise the children while he was away.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 106, 42, 'I’m going out.”', 'He confirmed his intention to leave the house.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 107, 43, '“Why should I go swearing to you?” Agafya laughed.', 'Agafya laughed at his demand, questioning why she needed to take an oath for him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 108, 43, '“I’ll look after them anyway.”', 'She reassured him that she would take care of the children regardless of an oath.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 109, 44, '“No, not unless you swear by the eternal salvation of your soul.', 'Kolya insisted on a specific, serious oath: one concerning the eternal salvation of her soul.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 110, 44, 'Otherwise I won’t go.”', 'He stated that he would not leave unless she made that sworn promise.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 111, 45, '“Don’t go, then.', 'Agafya responded with a simple dismissal, telling him to stay home.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 112, 45, 'I don’t care.', 'She indicated that his decision was indifferent to her.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 113, 45, 'It’s freezing out; stay home.”', 'She advised him to remain in the house because of the cold weather.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 114, 46, '“Squirts,” Kolya turned to the children, “this woman will stay with you till I come back, or till your mama comes, because she, too, should have been back long ago.', 'Kolya turned to the children and informed them that Agafya would look after them until either he or their mother returned, noting that their mother was already overdue.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 115, 46, 'And furthermore she will give you lunch.', 'He also told them that Agafya would be responsible for providing them with lunch.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 116, 46, 'Will you fix them something, Agafya?”', 'He directly asked Agafya if she would prepare their meal.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 117, 47, '“Could be.”', 'Agafya gave a brief, lukewarm confirmation that she might do so.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 118, 48, '“Good-bye, chicks, I’m going with an easy heart.', 'Kolya said farewell to the children, expressing that he was now leaving without worry.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 119, 48, 'And you, granny,” he said, imposingly and in a low voice, as he passed by Agafya, “spare their young years, don’t go telling them all your old wives’ nonsense about Katerina.', 'As he walked past Agafya, he spoke quietly but with authority, commanding her to protect the children\'s innocence by not sharing her foolish, fictional stories about Katerina\'s pregnancy.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 120, 48, 'Ici, Perezvon!”', 'He called the dog to follow him using the French command.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 121, 49, '“And you know where you can go!” Agafya snarled, this time in earnest.', 'Agafya responded with genuine anger, telling Kolya to leave abruptly.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 122, 49, '“Funny boy!', 'She called him a \"funny boy.\"', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-02', 123, 49, 'Ought to be whipped yourself for such talk, that’s what.”', 'She concluded that he was the one who deserved a whipping for the way he had spoken to her.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 1, 1, 'But Kolya was no longer listening.', 'Kolya had stopped paying attention to whatever was being said.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 2, 1, 'At last he was able to leave.', 'He was finally in a position to depart from the place he was in.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 3, 1, 'He walked out the gate, looked around, hunched his shoulders, and having said “Freezing!” set off straight down the street and then turned right down a lane to the mar- , ket square.', 'He exited the yard, observed his surroundings, reacted to the cold weather by saying \"Freezing!\", and began walking directly down the street before turning into a lane leading toward the market square.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 4, 1, 'When he reached the next to the last house before the square, he stopped at the gate, pulled a whistle out of his pocket, and whistled with all his might, as if giving a prearranged signal.', 'Near the market square, he paused at a specific gate, retrieved a whistle, and blew it very loudly, suggesting he was communicating a signal.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 5, 1, 'He did not have to wait more than a minute—a ruddy-cheeked boy of about eleven years old suddenly ran out to him through the gate, also wearing a warm, clean, and even stylish coat.', 'He waited only briefly before an eleven-year-old boy with a healthy, flushed face, wearing nice clothes, quickly emerged from the gate to meet him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 6, 1, 'This was the Smurov boy, who was in the preparatory class whereas Kolya Krasotkin was two years ahead, the son of a well-to-do official, whose parents evidently would not allow him to go around with Krasotkin, a notoriously desperate prankster, so that this time Smurov obviously had escaped on the sly.', 'The boy was identified as Smurov, who was in a lower school grade than Kolya, and was the son of a wealthy official; Smurov\'s parents, disliking Kolya\'s mischievous reputation, must have forbidden their son from seeing him, which means Smurov had sneaked out.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 7, 1, 'This Smurov, if the reader has not forgotten, was one of the group of boys who were throwing stones at Ilyusha across the ditch two months before, and had told Alyosha Karamazov then about Ilyusha.', 'The text reminds the reader that Smurov was one of the children involved in the previous incident of pelting Ilyusha with stones and was the one who later informed Alyosha Karamazov about Ilyusha.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 8, 2, '“I’ve been waiting a whole hour for you, Krasotkin,” Smurov said with a determined look, and the boys strode off towards the square.', 'Smurov stated seriously that he had been waiting a long time for Kolya, and they immediately began walking purposefully toward the market square.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 9, 3, '“I’m late,” Krasotkin replied.', 'Krasotkin acknowledged that he was behind schedule.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 10, 3, '“Circumstances arose.”', 'He gave a vague explanation that unforeseen events had caused his delay.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 11, 3, '“They won’t whip you for being with me?”', 'Krasotkin asked if Smurov would be punished physically for associating with him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 12, 4, '“Lord, no, they never whip me!', 'Smurov strongly denied that his parents ever use physical punishment on him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 13, 4, 'So you’ve brought Perezvon?”', 'Smurov then changed the topic to ask if Kolya had brought the dog, Perezvon.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 14, 5, '“Perezvon, too!”', 'Kolya confirmed that the dog Perezvon was also accompanying them.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 15, 6, '“He’s going there, too?”', 'Smurov inquired whether the dog was also intended to go to their destination.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 16, 7, '“He’s going, too.”', 'Kolya confirmed that Perezvon was going along with them.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 17, 8, '“Ah, if only it was Zhuchka!”', 'Smurov expressed a longing or wish that the dog they had was Zhuchka.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 18, 9, '“Impossible.', 'Kolya stated that the idea was not feasible.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 19, 9, 'Zhuchka does not exist.', 'Kolya declared that the dog Zhuchka no longer exists.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 20, 9, 'Zhuchka has vanished in the darkness of the unknown.”', 'He dramatically claimed that Zhuchka has completely disappeared or ceased to be.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 21, 10, '“Ah, couldn’t we do it?”', 'Smurov, suddenly stopping, proposed an alternative action.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 22, 10, 'Smurov suddenly stopped for a moment.', 'Smurov halted their progress momentarily.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 23, 10, '“Ilyusha did say that Zhuchka was shaggy, and gray and smoky, just like Perezvon— couldn’t we tell him it’s really Zhuchka?', 'He reasoned that since Ilyusha had described Zhuchka as shaggy, gray, and smoky—a description similar to Perezvon—they could try to convince Ilyusha that Perezvon is actually Zhuchka.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 24, 10, 'Maybe he’ll even believe it?”', 'He wondered if Ilyusha might accept the deception.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 25, 11, '“Schoolboy, do not stoop to lying, first; and second, not even for a good cause.', 'Kolya lectured Smurov, telling him he should never lie, even if the intention is good.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 26, 11, 'And above all, I hope you didn’t tell them anything about my coming.”', 'Kolya emphasized that he hoped Smurov had not disclosed his plan to visit.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 27, 12, '“God forbid, I know what I’m doing.', 'Smurov strongly assured Kolya that he knew better and had kept Kolya\'s visit a secret.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 28, 12, 'But you won’t comfort him with Perezvon,” sighed Smurov.', 'Smurov expressed his doubt that Perezvon would successfully cheer up Ilyusha.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 29, 12, '“You know, his father, the captain, I mean, the whiskbroom, told us he was going to bring him a puppy today, a real mastiff, with a black nose; he thinks he can comfort Ilyusha with it, only it’s not likely.”', 'Smurov shared that Ilyusha\'s father whom he mockingly calls \"the whiskbroom\" planned to bring Ilyusha a new, specific puppy, believing it would help, but Smurov doubted its effectiveness.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 30, 13, '“And Ilyusha himself—how is he?”', 'Kolya shifted the topic to ask about Ilyusha\'s current health condition.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 31, 14, '“Ah, he’s bad, bad!', 'Smurov replied with strong confirmation that Ilyusha is in very poor health.', '2026-07-18 15:50:05', '2026-07-18 15:50:05');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 32, 14, 'I think he has consumption.', 'Smurov stated his belief that Ilyusha is suffering from tuberculosis.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 33, 14, 'He’s quite conscious, only he keeps breathing, breathing, it’s not healthy the way he breathes.', 'He noted that Ilyusha is mentally aware but his persistent, unhealthy breathing indicates illness.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 34, 14, 'The other day he asked to be walked around the room, they put his boots on, he tried to walk but kept falling down.', 'He recalled a recent incident where Ilyusha requested a walk, but was too weak to stand and kept falling when attempting to walk.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 35, 14, 'Ah,’ he said, ‘I told you my old boots were no good, papa, even before I had trouble walking in them.’', 'Ilyusha had blamed his difficulty walking on his old boots, reminding his father that he had complained about them previously.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 36, 14, 'He thought he was stumbling because of his boots, but it was simply weakness.', 'Smurov clarifies that Ilyusha misinterpreted his stumbling, attributing it to his footwear when it was actually due to physical weakness.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 37, 14, 'He won’t live another week.', 'Smurov gave a grim prognosis, predicting Ilyusha would die within a week.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 38, 14, 'Herzenstube keeps coming.', 'He mentioned that the doctor, Herzenstube, continues to visit Ilyusha.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 39, 14, 'They’re rich again now, they’ve got a lot of money.”', 'Smurov added that Ilyusha\'s family is currently financially well-off.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 40, 15, '“Swindlers.”', 'Kolya\'s one-word reply to the mention of Herzenstube and wealth was an accusation of deceit.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 41, 16, '“Who are swindlers?”', 'Smurov asked for clarification on whom Kolya was referring to as swindlers.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 42, 17, '“Doctors, and all medical scum, generally speaking, and, naturally, in particular as well.', 'Kolya identified doctors and all medical professionals as swindlers, both as a group and individually.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 43, 17, 'I reject medicine.', 'He stated his outright dismissal of the value of medical science.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 44, 17, 'A useless institution.', 'He declared medicine to be an ineffective system.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 45, 17, 'But I’m still looking into all that.', 'He added that despite his rejection, he is still investigating these matters.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 46, 17, 'Anyway, what are these sentimentalities you’ve got going?', 'He abruptly changed the subject to question Smurov\'s apparent sentimentality.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 47, 17, 'Seems like your whole class is sitting there.”', 'He then observed that it seems Smurov\'s entire class is spending time at Ilyusha\'s house.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 48, 18, '“Not the whole class, but about ten of us always go there, every day.', 'Smurov corrected Kolya, stating that only about ten boys, not the entire class, visit daily.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 49, 18, 'It’s all right.”', 'He casually dismissed Kolya\'s judgment, implying the visits are fine.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 50, 19, '“What surprises me in all this is the role of Alexei Karamazov: his brother is going on trial tomorrow or the day after for such a crime, and he still finds so much time for sentimentalizing with boys!”', 'Kolya expressed surprise that Alexei Karamazov is spending so much time being sentimental with boys, especially since his brother is about to be tried for a major crime.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 51, 20, '“There isn’t any sentimentalizing in it.', 'Smurov denied that the activity involves any sentimentality.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 52, 20, 'You yourself are going now to make peace with Ilyusha.”', 'He pointed out Kolya\'s hypocrisy, stating that Kolya himself is on his way to reconcile with Ilyusha.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 53, 21, '“To make peace?', 'Kolya questioned Smurov\'s choice of words with surprise.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 54, 21, 'A funny expression.', 'He called the phrase \"to make peace\" ridiculous.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 55, 21, 'Incidentally, I allow no one to analyze my actions.”', 'He firmly stated that he does not permit anyone to interpret or judge his motives.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 56, 22, '“And Ilyusha will be so glad to see you!', 'Smurov expressed his belief that Ilyusha will be extremely happy about Kolya\'s arrival.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 57, 22, 'He doesn’t even dream that you’re coming.', 'He added that Ilyusha has no expectation of Kolya visiting.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 58, 22, 'Why, why wouldn’t you come for such a long time?”', 'Smurov then eagerly asked Kolya why he had delayed his visit for so long.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 59, 22, 'Smurov exclaimed with sudden ardor.', 'Smurov\'s question was delivered with a burst of passion.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 60, 23, '“That’s my business, my dear boy, not yours.', 'Kolya put Smurov in his place, saying his reasons for the delay were private.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 61, 23, 'I am going on my own, because such is my will, while you were all dragged there by Alexei Karamazov, so there’s a difference.', 'He distinguished his own visit as a voluntary act of will, contrasting it with Smurov\'s group, whom he claimed were merely led there by Alexei Karamazov, thus highlighting a difference between their motives.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 62, 23, 'And how do you know, maybe I’m not going to make peace at all?', 'He challenged Smurov\'s assumption about his purpose, suggesting his visit might not be for reconciliation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 63, 23, 'Silly expression!”', 'He reiterated his disdain for the phrase \"make peace.\"', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 64, 24, '“It wasn’t Karamazov at all, not him at all.', 'Smurov emphatically denied that Alexei Karamazov was the main reason for their visits.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 65, 24, 'Some of us just started going there by ourselves, of course with Karamazov at first.', 'He clarified that while Karamazov had initiated the visits, the boys were now continuing to go on their own.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 66, 24, 'And there was never anything like that, nothing silly.', 'Smurov defended their visits, stating they were not sentimental or foolish.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 67, 24, 'First one of us went, then another.', 'He described the visits as a gradual process where the boys started coming one by one.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 68, 24, 'His father was terribly glad to see us.', 'He noted that Ilyusha\'s father was extremely pleased to see the boys.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 69, 24, 'You know, he’ll just go out of his mind if Ilyusha dies.', 'Smurov expressed concern that Ilyusha\'s father would lose his sanity if his son passed away.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 70, 24, 'He can see Ilyusha’s going to die.', 'He mentioned that the father realizes Ilyusha\'s death is imminent.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 71, 24, 'But he’s so glad about us, that we made peace with Ilyusha.', 'The father\'s gladness stems from the reconciliation between the boys and Ilyusha.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 72, 24, 'Ilyusha asked about you, but he didn’t add anything more.', 'Smurov revealed that Ilyusha had inquired about Kolya, but said nothing further.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 73, 24, 'He just asks, and that’s all.', 'He emphasized that Ilyusha merely asked the question without elaborating.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 74, 24, 'His father will go out of his mind, or hang himself.', 'Smurov repeated his fear that Ilyusha\'s father would either go insane or commit suicide.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 75, 24, 'He’s acted crazy before.', 'He stated that the father has exhibited erratic behavior previously.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 76, 24, 'You know, he’s a noble man, and that was all a mistake.', 'Smurov defended Ilyusha\'s father, calling him honorable and suggesting the past incidents were misunderstandings.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 77, 24, 'It was the fault of that murderer, the one who gave him the beating.”', 'He attributed the past troubles to the individual who assaulted the father, calling the assailant a murderer.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 78, 25, '“Still, Karamazov is a riddle to me.', 'Kolya admitted that Alexei Karamazov\'s character remains a mystery to him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 79, 25, 'I could have made his acquaintance long ago, but I like to be proud in certain cases.', 'He explained that he deliberately avoided meeting Karamazov out of a desire to maintain his pride in some situations.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 80, 25, 'Besides, I’ve formed an opinion of him that still has to be verified and explained.”', 'Kolya concluded that he has a preliminary judgment of Karamazov that he still needs to confirm and fully understand.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 81, 26, 'Kolya fell imposingly silent; so did Smurov.', 'Kolya became quiet in a way that commanded attention, and Smurov followed suit.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 82, 26, 'Smurov, of course, stood in awe of Kolya Krasotkin and did not dare even think of rivaling him.', 'Smurov greatly admired Kolya and would never consider himself Kolya\'s equal.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 83, 26, 'And now he was terribly curious, because Kolya had explained that he was going “on his own,” and so there must be some riddle in the fact that Kolya had suddenly decided to go, and precisely on that day.', 'Smurov was intensely curious because Kolya\'s insistence on going \"on his own\" suggested a mysterious reason for his sudden decision to visit on that specific day.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 84, 26, 'They were crossing the market square, which at that hour was filled with farm wagons and lots of live fowl.', 'The boys were walking through the market area, which was currently bustling with wagons from farms and many live birds.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 85, 26, 'Town women were selling rolls, thread, and so forth, under their shed roofs.', 'Local women were selling small items like baked goods and thread from stalls sheltered by roofs.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 86, 26, 'In our town, such Sunday markets are naively called fairs, and there are many such fairs during the year.', 'The narrator notes that in this town, these regular Sunday markets are innocently referred to as fairs, which happen often throughout the year.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 87, 26, 'Perezvon ran along in the merriest spirits, constantly straying to right and left to smell something here and there.', 'Perezvon, the dog, was running happily, frequently moving side-to-side to sniff various objects.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 88, 26, 'When he met other dogs, he sniffed them with remarkable zeal, according to all canine rules.', 'Whenever Perezvon encountered other dogs, he followed typical dog behavior by sniffing them with great enthusiasm.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 89, 27, '“I like observing realism, Smurov,” Kolya suddenly spoke.', 'Kolya broke the silence to tell Smurov that he enjoys studying things as they are in reality.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 90, 27, '“Have you noticed how dogs sniff each other when they meet?', 'He drew Smurov\'s attention to the specific behavior of dogs sniffing upon meeting.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 91, 27, 'It must be some general law of their nature.”', 'Kolya theorized that this behavior must be a fundamental, universal rule of canine nature.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 92, 28, '“Yes, and a funny one, too.”', 'Smurov agreed with the observation and added that he finds the behavior amusing.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 93, 29, '“In fact, it is not a funny one, you’re wrong there.', 'Kolya contradicted Smurov, telling him he was mistaken that it was funny.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 94, 29, 'Nothing is funny in nature, however it may seem to man with his prejudices.', 'Kolya asserted that nothing in nature is truly funny, despite how human biases might perceive it.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 95, 29, 'If dogs could reason and criticize, they would undoubtedly find as much that is funny to them in the social relations of humans, their masters—if not far more; I repeat, because I am convinced of it, that there is far more foolishness in us.', 'Kolya argued that if dogs were rational and critical, they would find human social behavior just as or more ridiculous than humans find canine behavior, as he is convinced that humans possess far more foolishness.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 96, 29, 'That is Rakitin’s thought, a remarkable thought.', 'He credited this profound observation to Rakitin.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 97, 29, 'I am a socialist, Smurov.”', 'Kolya then declared his political ideology, stating he is a socialist.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 98, 30, '“And what is a socialist?” asked Smurov.', 'Smurov, unfamiliar with the term, asked Kolya for a definition of a socialist.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 99, 31, '“It’s when everyone is equal, everyone has property in common, there are no marriages, and each one has whatever religion and laws he likes, and all the rest.', 'Kolya explained socialism as a system where all people are equal, property is shared communally, marriage does not exist, and individuals are free to choose their own religion and laws.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 100, 31, 'You’re not grown up enough for that yet, you’re too young.', 'He then told Smurov that he was too immature to fully grasp the concept.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 101, 31, 'It is cold, by the way.”', 'Kolya abruptly commented that the weather was cold.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 102, 32, '“Yes.', 'Smurov agreed that it was cold.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 103, 32, 'Twelve degrees of frost.', 'He specified the temperature, noting it was twelve degrees below freezing.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 104, 32, 'My father just looked at the thermometer.”', 'He provided the source of his information, saying his father had checked the thermometer.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 105, 33, '“And have you noticed, Smurov, that in the middle of winter, when there are fifteen or even eighteen degrees of frost, it doesn’t seem as cold as it does now, for example, in the beginning of winter, if there’s suddenly an unexpected cold snap, like now, of twelve degrees, especially when there isn’t much snow.', 'Kolya pointed out that a moderate cold snap early in winter like the current twelve degrees, especially without much snow, feels colder than more severe temperatures later in the season.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 106, 33, 'It means people aren’t used to it yet.', 'He suggested that the reason for this difference in perceived coldness is a lack of acclimatization.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 107, 33, 'Everything is habit with people, everything, even state and political relations.', 'Kolya generalized that human actions and systems, including governance and politics, are driven entirely by habit.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 108, 33, 'Habit is the chief motive force.', 'He asserted that habit is the most important driving power in human life.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 109, 33, 'What a funny peasant, by the way.”', 'Kolya then abruptly drew attention to a peasant nearby, finding him amusing.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 110, 34, 'Kolya pointed to a stalwart peasant in a sheepskin coat, with a good-natured face, who was standing beside his wagon clapping his hands in their mittens to keep them warm.', 'Kolya indicated a physically strong, kind-faced peasant standing by his cart, trying to warm his hands by clapping them while wearing mittens.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 111, 34, 'His long, light brown beard was all hoary with frost.', 'The peasant\'s beard was covered with a white layer of frost.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 112, 35, '“The peasant’s got his beard frozen!” Kolya cried loudly and pertly as he passed by him.', 'As he walked past the man, Kolya loudly and cheekily called out a comment about the peasant\'s frozen beard.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 113, 36, '“Many have got their beards frozen,” the peasant uttered calmly and sententiously in reply.', 'The peasant responded with a calm, moralizing statement that many people share the condition of having a frozen beard.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 114, 37, '“Don’t pick on him,” Smurov remarked.', 'Smurov advised Kolya to leave the peasant alone.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 115, 38, '“It’s all right, he won’t be angry, he’s a nice fellow.', 'Kolya dismissed Smurov\'s concern, saying the peasant would not be offended and was a pleasant man.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 116, 38, 'Good-bye, Matvey.”', 'Kolya then addressed the peasant directly, using the name Matvey to say goodbye.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 117, 39, '“Good-bye.”', 'The peasant returned the farewell.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 118, 40, '“Are you really Matvey?”', 'Kolya, perhaps having guessed the name, asked if the peasant\'s name was actually Matvey.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 119, 41, '“I am.', 'The peasant confirmed that his name was Matvey.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 120, 41, 'Didn’t you know?”', 'He asked Kolya if he hadn\'t known this already.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 121, 42, '“No, I just said it.”', 'Kolya admitted that he had simply spoken the name without knowing if it was correct.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 122, 43, '“Well, I declare.', 'The peasant expressed surprise.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 123, 43, 'You must be one of them schoolboys.”', 'He correctly identified Kolya as a schoolboy.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 124, 44, '“One of them schoolboys.”', 'Kolya confirmed his identity.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 125, 45, '“And what, do they whip you?”', 'The peasant then asked if schoolboys like Kolya were subjected to physical punishment.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 126, 46, '“Not really, so-so.”', 'Kolya gave a non-committal answer, implying it sometimes happens.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 127, 47, '“Does it hurt?”', 'The peasant asked if being whipped was painful.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 128, 48, '“It can.”', 'Kolya replied that it is possible for it to hurt.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 129, 49, '“E-eh, that’s life!” the peasant sighed from the bottom of his heart.', 'The peasant responded with a deep, heartfelt sigh, accepting the possibility of pain as a part of life.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 130, 50, '“Good-bye, Matvey.”', 'Kolya repeated his farewell to the peasant.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 131, 51, '“Good-bye.', 'The peasant said goodbye again.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 132, 51, 'You’re a nice lad, that’s what.”', 'He added that he thought Kolya was a pleasant boy.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 133, 52, 'The boys walked on.', 'Kolya and Smurov continued their journey.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 134, 53, '“A good peasant,” Kolya began saying to Smurov.', 'Kolya commented to Smurov that the peasant was a fine man.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 135, 53, '“I like talking with the people, and am always glad to do them justice.”', 'Kolya expressed his enjoyment in conversing with common folk and his readiness to acknowledge their merits.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 136, 54, '“Why did you lie about them whipping us at school?” asked Smurov.', 'Smurov questioned why Kolya had falsely told the peasant that schoolboys are whipped.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 137, 55, '“But I had to comfort him.”', 'Kolya\'s explanation was that the lie was necessary to soothe the peasant.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 138, 56, '“How so?”', 'Smurov asked for clarification on how the lie would be comforting.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 139, 57, '“You know, Smurov, I don’t like it when people keep asking questions, when they don’t understand the first time.', 'Kolya expressed irritation at Smurov\'s lack of immediate understanding.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 140, 57, 'Some things can’t even be explained.', 'He implied that his reasons were too subtle or complex to be put into words.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 141, 57, 'A peasant’s notion is that schoolboys are whipped and ought to be whipped: what kind of schoolboy is he, if he isn’t whipped?', 'Kolya explained that peasants hold a belief that whipping is an expected and necessary part of a schoolboy\'s life.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 142, 57, 'And if I were suddenly to tell him that they don’t whip us in our school, it would upset him.', 'He reasoned that contradicting this belief would have disturbed the peasant.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 143, 57, 'Anyway, you don’t understand these things.', 'Kolya concluded that Smurov lacked the sophistication to grasp these subtleties.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 144, 57, 'One has to know how to talk with the people.”', 'He stated that engaging with the common folk requires a specific, skilled approach.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 145, 58, '“Only please don’t pick on them, or there’ll be another incident like that time with the goose.”', 'Smurov pleaded with Kolya to stop provoking people, warning that it might lead to a problematic event similar to one involving a goose.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 146, 59, '“Are you afraid?”', 'Kolya asked Smurov if he was scared.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 147, 59, '“Don’t laugh, Kolya.', 'Smurov requested Kolya not to mock him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 148, 59, 'I am afraid, by God.', 'He swore that he was indeed frightened.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 149, 59, 'My father will be terribly angry.', 'He expressed concern that his father would be extremely upset.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 150, 59, 'I’m strictly forbidden to go around with you.”', 'Smurov confessed that he was under strict parental orders not to associate with Kolya.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 151, 60, '“Don’t worry, nothing will happen this time.', 'Kolya reassured Smurov that there would be no trouble on this occasion.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 152, 60, 'Hello, Natasha,” he shouted to one of the market women under the shed.', 'Kolya then called out a greeting using the name Natasha to a woman selling goods under a shelter.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 153, 61, '“Natasha, is it?', 'The woman questioned Kolya\'s use of the name Natasha.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 154, 61, 'My name’s Maria,” the woman, who was still far from old, replied in a shrill voice.', 'The woman, who was still young, replied in a high-pitched voice, stating her name was Maria.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 155, 62, '“Maria!', 'Kolya repeated her name.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 156, 62, 'How nice!', 'He commented on how pleasant her name was.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 157, 62, 'Good-bye.”', 'He then immediately said goodbye.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 158, 63, '“Ah, the scamp!', 'The woman exclaimed, calling Kolya a rogue.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 159, 63, 'Knee-high to a mushroom and he’s at it already!”', 'She commented that Kolya was still a small child but was already getting into mischief.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 160, 64, '“No time, I have no time for you now, tell me next Sunday,” Kolya waved his hand at her, as if he was not bothering her but she him.', 'Kolya dismissed her, claiming he was busy and asking her to talk next week, behaving as if she was the one pestering him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 161, 65, '“What am I going to tell you next Sunday?', 'Maria questioned why she would have anything to tell him the following week.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 162, 65, 'I’m not pestering you, you’re pestering me, you rascal,” Maria went on shouting, “you ought to be whipped, that’s what, you’re a famous offender, that’s what!”', 'She continued shouting, correcting him that he was the one harassing her, calling him a rascal and a notorious troublemaker who deserved a beating.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 163, 66, 'There was laughter among the other market women, who were selling things from their stands next to Maria, when suddenly, from under the arcade of shops nearby, for no reason at all an irritated man jumped out, who looked like a shop clerk, but a stranger, not one of our tradesmen, in a long blue caftan and a visored cap, a young man, with dark brown, curly hair and a long, pale, slightly pockmarked face.', 'The other women sellers nearby laughed at the exchange, which was interrupted by a seemingly random, annoyed man who suddenly emerged from a nearby covered area, appearing to be a shop clerk but not a local one, wearing a long blue coat and a cap, and having dark, curly hair and a long, pale, slightly scarred face.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 164, 66, 'He was somehow absurdly agitated, and at once began threatening Kolya with his fist.', 'The man was inexplicably and foolishly excited and immediately started shaking his fist aggressively at Kolya.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 165, 67, '“I know you,” he kept exclaiming irritably, “I know you!”', 'The man repeatedly and angrily shouted that he recognized Kolya.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 166, 68, 'Kolya stared fixedly at him.', 'Kolya focused his gaze intently on the man.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 167, 68, 'He was unable to recall when he could have had any quarrel with this man.', 'Kolya could not remember ever having an argument with this specific person.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 168, 68, 'But he had had so many quarrels in the streets that he could not remember them all.', 'He conceded that he had been in too many street altercations to recall every single one.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 169, 69, '“So you know me?” he asked ironically.', 'Kolya responded with a mocking question, confirming the man\'s claim of recognition.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 170, 70, '“I know you!', 'The tradesman affirmed his recognition.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 171, 70, 'I know you!” the tradesman kept repeating like a fool.', 'The man continued to state this fact repeatedly and senselessly.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 172, 71, '“So much the better for you.', 'Kolya sarcastically suggested that knowing him was an advantage for the man.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 173, 71, 'But I am in a hurry.', 'He stated that he was pressed for time.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 174, 71, 'Good-bye.”', 'Kolya then bid him farewell.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 175, 72, '“You’re still up to your tricks?” the tradesman shouted.', 'The tradesman yelled a question asking if Kolya was still behaving mischievously.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 176, 72, '“Up to your tricks again?', 'He repeated the question of whether Kolya was repeating his past pranks.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 177, 72, 'I know you!', 'He reiterated that he knew Kolya.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 178, 72, 'So you’re up to your tricks again?”', 'He questioned again if Kolya was back to his old ways.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 179, 73, '“It’s none of your business, brother, what tricks I’m up to,” Kolya said, stopping and continuing to examine him.', 'Kolya stopped walking and, while observing the man, told him that his mischievous activities were not the man\'s concern.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 180, 74, '“None of my business, is it?”', 'The man questioned Kolya\'s assertion.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 181, 75, '“That’s right, it’s none of your business.”', 'Kolya confirmed that the matter was not the man\'s affair.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 182, 76, '“And whose is it?', 'The man demanded to know whose business it was, if not his own.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 183, 76, 'Whose?', 'He repeated the question.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 184, 76, 'Well, whose?”', 'He insisted on an answer.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 185, 77, '“It’s Trifon Nikitich’s business now, brother, not yours.”', 'Kolya gave a specific name, Trifon Nikitich, claiming the matter was his concern now, not the man\'s.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 186, 78, '“What Trifon Nikitich?” the fellow stared at Kolya in foolish surprise, though still with the same excitement.', 'The man reacted with a bewildered stare, asking who this Trifon Nikitich was, while still being absurdly agitated.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 187, 78, 'Kolya solemnly looked him up and down.', 'Kolya gave the man a serious, scrutinizing look.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 188, 79, '“Have you been to the Church of the Ascension?” he suddenly asked him sternly and insistently.', 'Kolya abruptly and seriously asked the man if he had visited the Church of the Ascension.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 189, 80, '“What Ascension?', 'The man seemed confused by the question.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 190, 80, 'Why?', 'He asked for the reason behind the question.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 191, 80, 'No, I haven’t,” the fellow was a bit taken aback.', 'The man replied that he had not been, clearly startled by the line of questioning.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 192, 80, '“Do you know Sabaneyev?” Kolya went on, still more insistently and sternly.', 'Kolya continued his severe questioning, now asking if the man knew a person named Sabaneyev.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 193, 81, '“What Sabaneyev?', 'The man questioned which Sabaneyev Kolya was referring to.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 194, 81, 'No, I don’t know him.”', 'He stated that he did not know anyone by that name.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 195, 82, '“Devil take you, then!” Kolya suddenly snapped, and turning sharply to the right, quickly went his way as if scorning even to speak with such a dolt who does not even know Sabaneyev.', 'Kolya angrily cursed the man, then sharply turned and walked away quickly, acting as if the man were a fool not worth talking to because he was unfamiliar with \'Sabaneyev.\'', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 196, 83, '“Hey, wait!', 'The man called out, trying to stop Kolya.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 197, 83, 'What Sabaneyev?” the fellow came to his senses and again got all excited.', 'The man recovered his awareness and became agitated again, asking for the identity of Sabaneyev.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 198, 83, '“What’s he talking about?” he suddenly turned to the market women, staring foolishly at them.', 'He then turned to the women sellers, asking them what Kolya had been referring to, looking bewildered.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 199, 84, 'The women burst out laughing.', 'The women reacted to the man\'s confusion by laughing loudly.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 200, 84, '“A clever boy,” one of them said.', 'One of the women commented that Kolya was a smart boy.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 201, 85, '“What, what Sabaneyev did he mean?” the fellow kept repeating frenziedly, waving his right hand.', 'The man continued to ask frantically about the identity of Sabaneyev, gesticulating with his hand.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 202, 86, '“Ah, it must be the Sabaneyev that worked for the Kuzmichevs, must be that one,” one woman suddenly understood.', 'One of the women suddenly realized who Kolya must have been referring to, suggesting it was a Sabaneyev who had been employed by the Kuzmichev family.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 203, 87, 'The fellow stared wildly at her.', 'The man looked at the woman with an intense, confused gaze.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 204, 88, '“For the Kuz-mi-chevs?” another woman repeated.', 'A second woman questioned the employer\'s name, repeating it slowly.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 205, 88, '“He’s no Trifon.', 'She then argued that this person was not named Trifon.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 206, 88, 'That one’s Kuzma, not Trifon, and the boy said Trifon Nikitich, so it’s somebody else.”', 'She reasoned that the person working for the Kuzmichevs was named Kuzma, not Trifon, and since Kolya had specified Trifon Nikitich, it must be a different person.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 207, 89, '“No, he’s no Trifon, and he’s no Sabaneyev either, he’s Chizhov,” a third woman suddenly joined in, who up to then had been silent and listening seriously.', 'A third woman, who had been listening intently without speaking, interjected to say that the person was neither Trifon nor Sabaneyev, but Chizhov.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 208, 89, '“His name’s Alexei Ivanich.', 'She provided his full name, Alexei Ivanich.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 209, 89, 'Alexei Ivanich Chizhov.”', 'She repeated the full name.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 210, 90, '“That’s right, he is Chizhov,” a fourth woman confirmed emphatically.', 'A fourth woman strongly agreed that the man\'s name was indeed Chizhov.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 211, 91, 'The stunned fellow kept looking from one woman to another.', 'The bewildered man repeatedly turned his gaze from one woman to the next.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 212, 91, '“But why did he ask me, why did he ask me, good people?” he kept exclaiming, now almost in despair.', 'The man, now close to panic, desperately asked the women why Kolya had questioned him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 213, 91, '‘“Do you know Sabaneyev?’', 'He quoted Kolya\'s question about Sabaneyev.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 214, 91, 'Devil knows who Sabaneyev is!”', 'He exclaimed that he had no idea who Sabaneyev was.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 215, 92, '“What a muddlehead!', 'One woman called the man a confused idiot.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 216, 92, 'Didn’t you hear, it’s not Sabaneyev, it’s Chizhov, Alexei Ivanich Chizhov, that’s who!” one of the market women shouted at him imposingly.', 'She shouted sternly that the person Kolya meant was Chizhov, not Sabaneyev, giving the full name.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 217, 93, '“What Chizhov?', 'The man asked for clarification on which Chizhov was being discussed.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 218, 93, 'Who is he?', 'He asked for the person\'s identity.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 219, 93, 'Tell me, if you know.”', 'He requested the woman to identify Chizhov if she knew him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 220, 94, '“A tall, snot-nosed fellow, he used to sit in the marketplace last summer.”', 'She described Chizhov as a tall, runny-nosed man who had been a regular presence in the marketplace the previous summer.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 221, 95, '“What the hell do I need your Chizhov for, eh, good people?”', 'The man, frustrated, demanded to know why he should care about this Chizhov.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 222, 96, '“How do I know what the hell you need Chizhov for?”', 'The woman replied that she could not possibly know what the man\'s interest in Chizhov was.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 223, 97, '“Who knows what you need him for?” another woman joined in.', 'A second woman echoed the first, asking rhetorically why they would know the man\'s needs.', '2026-07-18 15:50:06', '2026-07-18 15:50:06');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 224, 97, '“You should know what you need him for, it’s you doing all the squawking.', 'She asserted that since the man was the one complaining, he should know his own motives.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 225, 97, 'He was speaking to you, not to us, fool that you are.', 'She reminded the man that Kolya\'s questions were directed at him, not them, calling him a fool.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 226, 97, 'So you really don’t know him?”', 'She then asked if he truly did not know Chizhov.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 227, 98, '“Who?”', 'The man asked for the name again.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 228, 99, '“Chizhov.”', 'The woman repeated the name Chizhov.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 229, 100, '“Ah, devil take Chizhov, and you along with him!', 'The man cursed both Chizhov and the woman.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 230, 100, 'I’ll give him a thrashing, that’s what!', 'He threatened that he would beat Chizhov.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 231, 100, 'He was laughing at me!”', 'He claimed that Kolya was mocking him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 232, 101, '“You’ll give Chizhov a thrashing?', 'The woman questioned the man\'s ability to beat Chizhov.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 233, 101, 'More likely he’ll give you one!', 'She suggested that Chizhov was more likely to beat the man.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 234, 101, 'You’re a fool, that’s what!”', 'She emphatically called the man a fool.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 235, 102, '“Not Chizhov, not Chizhov, you wicked, nasty woman, I’ll thrash the boy, that’s what!', 'The man denied he meant Chizhov, insulted the woman, and then stated he would beat Kolya.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 236, 102, 'Let me have him, let me have him—he was laughing at me!”', 'He shouted that he wanted to catch Kolya because the boy had made fun of him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 237, 103, 'The women all roared with laughter.', 'All the market women found the man\'s outburst extremely funny and laughed loudly.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 238, 103, 'And Kolya was already far off, strutting along with a triumphant expression on his face.', 'Kolya was now a long distance away, walking with a proud and victorious look.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 239, 103, 'Smurov walked beside him, looking back at the group shouting far behind them.', 'Smurov was walking next to Kolya, watching the shouting group in the distance.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 240, 103, 'He, too, was having a good time, though he still feared getting into some scandal with Kolya.', 'Smurov was enjoying the incident, but he remained worried about getting into trouble because of Kolya.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 241, 104, '“What Sabaneyev were you asking him about?” he asked Kolya, guessing what the answer would be.', 'Smurov asked Kolya the identity of the Sabaneyev he had mentioned, already suspecting the answer.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 242, 105, '“How do I know?', 'Kolya replied that he did not know who Sabaneyev was.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 243, 105, 'They’ll go on shouting till nighttime now.', 'He predicted that the people would continue arguing about the matter until the evening.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 244, 105, 'I like stirring up fools in all strata of society.', 'Kolya stated his enjoyment in provoking foolish people across different social classes.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 245, 105, 'There stands another dolt, that peasant there.', 'He pointed out another peasant, whom he also considered a fool.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 246, 105, 'People say, ‘There’s no one stupider than a stupid Frenchman,’ but note how the Russian physiognomy betrays itself.', 'Kolya referred to a common saying about French stupidity but suggested that the Russian face reveals similar foolishness.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 247, 105, 'Isn’t it written all over that peasant’s face that he’s a fool, eh?”', 'He asked Smurov for confirmation that the peasant\'s face clearly showed his lack of intelligence.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 248, 106, '“Leave him alone, Kolya.', 'Smurov advised Kolya to stop bothering the peasant.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 249, 106, 'Let’s keep going.”', 'He urged Kolya to continue their walk.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 250, 107, '“No, now that I’ve gotten started, I wouldn’t stop for the world.', 'Kolya refused, saying he was committed to his course of action and would not stop now.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 251, 107, 'Hey!', 'He called out to the peasant.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 252, 107, 'Good morning, peasant!”', 'He wished the peasant a good morning.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 253, 108, 'A burly peasant, who was slowly passing by and seemed to have had a drop to drink already, with a round, simple face and a beard streaked with gray, raised his head and looked at the lad.', 'A large, somewhat inebriated peasant with a simple, round face and a gray-flecked beard, who was walking slowly past, looked up at Kolya.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 254, 109, '“Well, good morning, if you’re not joking,” he answered unhurriedly.', 'The peasant replied calmly, returning the greeting on the condition that Kolya was serious.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 255, 110, '“And if I am joking?” laughed Kolya.', 'Kolya laughed and questioned what would happen if he were making a joke.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 256, 111, '“Joke then, if you’re joking, and God be with you.', 'The peasant permitted him to joke and wished him well.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 257, 111, 'Never mind, it’s allowed.', 'He said not to worry, as joking is acceptable.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 258, 111, 'A man can always have his joke.”', 'He stated that a person is always entitled to make a joke.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 259, 112, '“Sorry, brother, I was joking.”', 'Kolya apologized for joking and confirmed he had not been serious.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 260, 113, '“So, God will forgive you.”', 'The peasant replied that God would pardon him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 261, 114, '“But you, do you forgive me?”', 'Kolya then asked if the peasant himself forgave him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 262, 115, '“That I do.', 'The peasant confirmed that he forgave Kolya.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 263, 115, 'Run along now.”', 'He then told Kolya to be on his way.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 264, 116, '“Look here, you seem to be a smart peasant.”', 'Kolya commented that the peasant seemed intelligent.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 265, 117, '“Smarter than you,” the peasant replied unexpectedly, and with the same air of importance.', 'The peasant unexpectedly claimed to be more intelligent than Kolya, maintaining his serious demeanor.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 266, 118, '“That’s unlikely,” Kolya was somewhat taken aback.', 'Kolya, surprised by the claim, stated that he doubted it was true.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 267, 119, '“It’s the truth I’m telling you.”', 'The peasant insisted that he was speaking the truth.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 268, 120, '“Well, maybe it is.”', 'Kolya conceded that the peasant might be telling the truth.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 269, 121, '“So there, brother.”', 'The peasant made a final statement, accepting Kolya\'s concession.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 270, 122, '“Good-bye, peasant.”', 'Kolya said goodbye to the peasant.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 271, 123, '“Good-bye.”', 'The peasant returned the farewell.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 272, 124, '“Peasants differ,” Kolya observed to Smurov after some silence.', 'Kolya broke the silence to comment to Smurov that peasants are not all the same.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 273, 124, '“How was I to know I’d run into a smart one?', 'He questioned how he could have foreseen encountering an intelligent peasant.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 274, 124, 'I’m always prepared to recognize intelligence in the people.”', 'He claimed that he is always ready to acknowledge the intelligence of common folk.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 275, 125, 'Far away the cathedral clock struck half past eleven.', 'A clock in the distance, presumably from the cathedral, chimed to indicate it was 11:30 AM.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 276, 125, 'The boys began to hurry, and covered the rest of the still quite long way to Captain Snegiryov’s house quickly and now almost without speaking.', 'Realizing the time, the boys increased their pace, covering the remaining long distance to Captain Snegiryov\'s house rapidly and mostly in silence.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 277, 125, 'Twenty paces from the house, Kolya stopped and told Smurov to go on ahead and call Karamazov out to meet him there.', 'About twenty steps away from the house, Kolya halted and instructed Smurov to go inside and ask Karamazov to come out to meet him at that spot.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 278, 125, '“For some preliminary sniffing,” he observed to Smurov.', 'Kolya told Smurov that he wanted Karamazov to come out for an initial assessment or sizing-up.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 279, 125, '“But why call him out?” Smurov tried to object.', 'Smurov attempted to argue against Kolya\'s demand, asking why Karamazov needed to be called outside.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 280, 125, '“Just go in, they’ll be terribly glad to see you.', 'He suggested that Kolya should simply enter, as his arrival would be greatly welcomed.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 281, 125, 'Why do you want to get acquainted in the freezing cold?”', 'Smurov questioned the necessity of making their acquaintance outside in the cold weather.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('10-03', 282, 125, '“It’s for me to know why I need him here, in the freezing cold,” Kolya snapped despotically as he was terribly fond of doing with these “little boys”, and Smurov ran to carry out the order.', 'Kolya replied with a dominating, sharp tone characteristic of how he liked to treat younger boys, stating that his reasons for needing Karamazov there were his own, and Smurov immediately ran off to obey the command.', '2026-07-18 15:50:07', '2026-07-18 15:50:07');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 1, 1, 'I am not a doctor, but nevertheless I feel the moment has come when it is decidedly necessary for me to explain to the reader at least something of the nature of Ivan Fyodorovich’s illness.', 'The narrator admits a lack of medical expertise but feels compelled to describe Ivan\'s deteriorating condition to help the reader understand the upcoming events.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 2, 1, 'Getting ahead of myself, I will say only one thing: he was, that evening, precisely just on the verge of brain fever, which finally took complete possession of his organism, long in disorder but stubbornly refusing to succumb.', 'Foreshadowing Ivan\'s collapse, the narrator explains that on this night, Ivan\'s long-resisted physical and mental breakdown was finally overwhelming him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 3, 1, 'Though I know nothing of medicine, I will venture the suggestion that he had indeed succeeded, perhaps, by a terrible effort of will, in postponing his illness for a time, hoping, of course, to overcome it completely.', 'The narrator guesses that Ivan had used sheer willpower to delay the onset of his sickness, aiming to fight it off entirely.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 4, 1, 'He knew he was not well, but he was loath to be ill at that time, during those approaching fatal moments of his life; he had to be personally present, to speak his word boldly and resolutely, and “vindicate himself to himself. “', 'Ivan was aware of his illness but refused to succumb because he needed to be present for an upcoming trial to speak his truth and prove his resolve.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 5, 1, 'However, he did once visit the new doctor who had come from Moscow, invited by Katerina Ivanovna owing to a fantasy of hers, which I have already mentioned above.', 'Despite his stubbornness, Ivan had recently consulted a new Moscow doctor, whose presence was requested by Katerina Ivanovna due to her own whims.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 6, 1, 'The doctor, having listened to him and examined him, concluded that he was indeed suffering from something like a brain disorder, as it were, and was not at all surprised at a certain confession that he made to him, though not without repugnance.', 'The doctor diagnosed Ivan with a preliminary brain condition and was unfazed by Ivan\'s reluctant admission, likely concerning his hallucinations.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 7, 1, '“In your condition hallucinations are quite possible,” the doctor decided, “though they should be verified ... but generally it is necessary to begin serious treatment without a moment’s delay, otherwise things will go badly.”', 'The doctor warned Ivan that his state made hallucinations likely and urged him to start immediate medical treatment to avoid severe consequences.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 8, 1, 'But Ivan Fyodorovich, having left the doctor, did not follow up this sensible advice, and treated the idea of treatment with disregard: “I’m up and about, I’m still strong enough, if I collapse it’s another matter, then anyone who likes can treat me,” he decided, with a wave of the hand.', 'Ivan ignored the medical advice, deciding that as long as he could still function physically, he would not bother with treatment until he completely collapsed.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 9, 1, 'And so he was sitting there now, almost aware of being delirious, and, as I have already said, peering persistently at some object on the sofa against the opposite wall.', 'Currently, Ivan sits in his room, semi-conscious of his own delirium, staring intently at something on the facing sofa.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 10, 1, 'Someone suddenly turned out to be sitting there, though God knows how he had got in, because he had not been in the room when Ivan Fyodorovich came back from seeing Smerdyakov.', 'A mysterious figure appears on the sofa, seemingly out of nowhere, as the room was empty when Ivan returned from his meeting with Smerdyakov.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 11, 1, 'It was some gentleman, or, rather, a certain type of Russian gentleman, no longer young, qui frisait la cinquantaine,303 as the French say, with not too much gray in his dark, rather long, and still thick hair, and with a pointed beard.', 'The apparition takes the form of a middle-aged, quintessential Russian gentleman—around fifty years old—sporting dark, thick hair with slight graying and a pointed beard.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 12, 1, 'He was wearing a sort of brown jacket, evidently from the best of tailors, but already shabby, made approximately three years ago and already completely out of fashion, such as no well-to-do man of society had been seen in for at least two years.', 'The man\'s clothing—a once-expensive but now worn and outdated brown jacket—suggests a decline in his financial or social status.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 13, 1, 'His linen, his long, scarflike necktie, all was just what every stylish gentleman would wear, but, on closer inspection, the linen was a bit dirty and the wide scarf was quite threadbare.', 'While his accessories aim for a stylish appearance, looking closely reveals that they are unwashed and worn out, further emphasizing his faded elegance.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 14, 1, 'The visitor’s checkered trousers fitted perfectly, but again they were too light and somehow too narrow, of a style no one wore any longer, as was the soft, downy white hat the visitor had brought with him, though it was entirely the wrong season.', 'His well-fitting but out-of-style pants and out-of-season white hat highlight a lingering vanity mixed with an inability to keep up with current trends or practicalities.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 15, 1, 'In short, he gave the appearance of decency on rather slender means.', 'Overall, the visitor looks like someone desperately trying to maintain a respectable facade despite being impoverished.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 16, 1, 'The gentleman looked as though he belonged to the category of former idle landowners that flourished in the time of serfdom; had obviously seen the world and decent society, had once had connections and perhaps had them still, but, after the gay life of his youth and the recent abolition of serfdom, had gradually fallen into poverty and become a sort of sponger, in bon ton, as it were, knocking about among good old acquaintances, and received by them for his easy, agreeable nature, and also considering that he was, after all, a decent man, who could even be invited to sit at the table in any company, though, of course, in a humble place.', 'The hallucination represents an obsolete class of Russian aristocrats who lost their wealth after the emancipation of the serfs, now surviving as polite, tolerated freeloaders relying on old connections.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 17, 1, 'Such spongers, gentlemen of agreeable nature, who can tell a story or two and play a hand of cards, and who decidedly dislike having any tasks thrust upon them, are usually single, either bachelors or widowers, and if they have children, the children are always brought up somewhere far away, by some aunts, whom the gentleman hardly ever mentions in decent company, as though somewhat ashamed of such relations.', 'These types of moochers are typically unmarried, avoid real work, entertain their hosts with games, and are emotionally and physically estranged from any children they might have.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 18, 1, 'They gradually become estranged from their children altogether, occasionally receiving letters from them on their birthday or at Christmas, and sometimes even answering them.', 'Their relationship with their offspring is reduced to rare, superficial holiday correspondence.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 19, 1, 'The unexpected visitor’s physiognomy was not so much good-humored as, again, agreeable and ready, depending on the circumstances, for any amiable expression.', 'The visitor\'s face does not show genuine warmth, but rather a practiced, adaptive pleasantness designed to placate others.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 20, 1, 'He did not have a watch, but he had a tortoiseshell lorgnette on a black ribbon.', 'Lacking a practical timepiece, he instead carries a pretentious optical accessory, reflecting his skewed priorities.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 21, 1, 'On the middle finger of his right hand there was displayed a massive gold ring with an inexpensive opal.', 'He wears a flashy but cheap piece of jewelry, attempting to maintain the illusion of past wealth.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 22, 1, 'Ivan Fyodorovich was spitefully silent and did not want to begin talking.', 'Ivan refuses to initiate the conversation, feeling bitter and resentful toward the apparition.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 23, 1, 'The visitor sat and waited precisely like a sponger who had just come down from upstairs, from the room assigned to him, to keep his host company at tea, but was humbly silent, since the host was preoccupied and scowling at the thought of something; but who was ready for any amiable conversation as soon as the host would begin it.', 'The hallucination perfectly mimics the behavior of a submissive houseguest, waiting patiently for his moody host to acknowledge him before speaking.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 24, 1, 'Suddenly his face seemed to express some unexpected concern.', 'The visitor\'s expression shifts abruptly to one of feigned or sudden worry.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 25, 2, '“Listen,” he began to Ivan Fyodorovich, “forgive me, it’s just a reminder: didn’t you go to Smerdyakov to find out about Katerina Ivanovna?', 'The visitor politely interrupts Ivan\'s silence to remind him of his original, forgotten purpose for visiting Smerdyakov.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 26, 2, 'Yet you left without finding out anything about her, you must have forgotten...”', 'The apparition points out that Ivan got so distracted that he failed to ask about the very woman he went there to inquire about.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 27, 3, '“Ah, yes!” suddenly escaped from Ivan, and his face darkened with worry, “yes, I forgot ...', 'Ivan is startled and visibly distressed upon realizing the truth of the visitor\'s reminder.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 28, 3, 'Anyway, it’s all the same now, all till tomorrow,” he muttered to himself.', 'Ivan dismisses the oversight, deciding that it is too late to fix it tonight and it must wait until the next day.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 29, 3, '“As for you,” he turned irritably to his visitor, “I’d have remembered it myself in a moment, because that’s exactly what has been causing me such anguish!', 'Ivan angrily addresses the hallucination, claiming he was already subconsciously bothered by the forgotten task and would have remembered it independently.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 30, 3, 'Why did you have to come out with it?', 'Ivan questions the visitor\'s motive for bringing the matter up.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 31, 3, 'Do you think I’ll simply believe you prompted me and not that I remembered it myself?”', 'Ivan defiantly refuses to give the hallucination credit for the thought, insisting it originated from his own mind.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 32, 4, '“Don’t believe it then,” the gentleman smiled sweetly, “what good is faith by force?', 'The visitor responds pleasantly, arguing that belief cannot be genuinely compelled.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 33, 4, 'Besides, proofs are no help to faith, especially material proofs.', 'He asserts that physical evidence does not actually create true spiritual belief.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 34, 4, 'Thomas believed not because he saw the risen Christ but because he wanted to believe even before that.304', 'The visitor uses the biblical example of Doubting Thomas to suggest that the desire to believe precedes the acceptance of evidence.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 35, 4, 'Spiritualists, for example ... I like them so much ... imagine, they think they’re serving faith because devils show their little horns to them from the other world.', 'He mockingly praises spiritualists who mistakenly believe that interacting with minor demons validates true religious faith.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 36, 4, '‘This,’ they say, ‘is a material proof, so to speak, that the other world exists.’', 'He mimics the flawed logic of spiritualists who view supernatural manifestations as concrete evidence of the afterlife.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 37, 4, 'The other world and material proofs, la-di-da!', 'The visitor scoffs at the very concept of applying physical proof to metaphysical realms.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 38, 4, 'And, after all, who knows whether proof of the devil is also a proof of God?', 'He raises a philosophical paradox, questioning if evidence of evil inherently proves the existence of a divine creator.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 39, 4, 'I want to join an idealist society and form an opposition within it: ‘I’m a realist,’ I’ll say, ‘not a materialist,’ heh, heh!”', 'The visitor chuckles at his own joke about joining a philosophical group only to adopt a contrarian, nuanced position.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 40, 5, '“Listen,” Ivan Fyodorovich suddenly got up from the table.', 'Ivan abruptly stands up, showing his mounting agitation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 41, 5, '“I seem to be delirious now ... and of course I am delirious ... you can lie as much as you like, it’s all the same to me!', 'Ivan openly acknowledges his madness and tells the hallucination that its words hold no power over him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 42, 5, 'You won’t put me into a rage, as you did last time.', 'He resolves not to let the apparition provoke his anger as it had during a previous episode.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 43, 5, 'Only I’m ashamed of something ... I feel like pacing the room ... I sometimes don’t see you, and don’t even hear your voice, as last time, but I always guess what you’re driveling, because i is I, I myself who am talking, and not you!', 'Ivan admits a sense of shame, recognizing that the visitor\'s words are merely reflections of his own subconscious thoughts.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 44, 5, 'Only I don’t know whether I was asleep last time or actually saw you.', 'Ivan expresses confusion over the boundaries of his previous hallucinations, unsure if they occurred in a dream or while awake.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 45, 5, 'I am now going to wet a towel with cold water and put it to my head, and maybe you’ll evaporate.”', 'Seeking a practical remedy to clear his mind, Ivan declares his intention to use a cold compress to banish the illusion.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 46, 6, 'Ivan Fyodorovich went to the corner, took a towel, carried out his intention, and with the wet towel on his head began pacing up and down the room.', 'Ivan physically performs the action he just described, hoping the cold towel and movement will ground him in reality.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 47, 7, '“I’m glad we can be so informal with each other,” the visitor tried to begin.', 'The apparition attempts to strike up a casual conversation, interpreting Ivan\'s actions as a sign of comfortable familiarity.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 48, 8, '“Fool,” Ivan laughed, “what, should I call you ‘sir’ or something?', 'Ivan mocks the visitor\'s attempt at civility, pointing out the absurdity of respecting a figment of his imagination.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 49, 8, 'I feel fine now, only there’s a pain in my temple ... and in the top of my head ... only please don’t philosophize, as you did last time.', 'Ivan notes a slight physical improvement alongside lingering head pains, and demands the visitor refrain from philosophical arguments.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 50, 8, 'Tell some pleasant lies, if you can’t clear out.', 'Accepting that he cannot easily banish the hallucination, Ivan asks it to at least be entertaining.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 51, 8, 'Gossip, since you’re a sponger, go ahead and gossip.', 'Leaning into the visitor\'s persona as a social freeloader, Ivan invites him to share trivial rumors.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 52, 8, 'Why am I stuck with such a nightmare!', 'Ivan laments his unfortunate mental state and the specific, annoying form his hallucination has taken.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 53, 8, 'But I’m not afraid of you.', 'Ivan asserts his courage, refusing to be intimidated by his own mind.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 54, 8, 'I will overcome you.', 'He vows to conquer his illness and the delusions it brings.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 55, 8, 'They won’t take me to the madhouse!”', 'Ivan expresses his deep fear of being institutionalized, determined to maintain his sanity.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 56, 9, '“C’est charmant—sponger!', 'The visitor is amused and delighted by the label Ivan has given him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 57, 9, 'Yes, that is precisely my aspect.', 'He agrees that the persona of a freeloader perfectly captures his current manifestation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 58, 9, 'What am I on earth if not a sponger?', 'The visitor rhetorically asks what other role a lingering spirit could possibly play in the human world.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 59, 9, 'Incidentally, I’m a little surprised listening to you: by God, it seems you’re gradually beginning to take me for something real, and not just your fantasy, as you insisted last time ...”', 'The apparition playfully points out that Ivan\'s intense emotional engagement suggests he is starting to believe the visitor is real.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 60, 10, '“Not for a single moment do I take you for the real truth,” Ivan cried, somehow even furiously.', 'Ivan aggressively denies giving the apparition any reality, becoming enraged at the suggestion.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 61, 10, '“You are a lie, you are my illness, you are a ghost.', 'He reinforces his rational understanding by explicitly defining the visitor as a mere symptom and falsehood.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 62, 10, 'Only I don’t know how to destroy you, and I see I’ll have to suffer through it for a while.', 'Ivan admits his helplessness in making the hallucination disappear, resigning himself to enduring it temporarily.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 63, 10, 'You are my hallucination.', 'He repeats his diagnosis to anchor himself to reality.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 64, 10, 'You are the embodiment of myself, but of just one side of me ... of my thoughts and feelings, but only the most loathsome and stupid of them.', 'Ivan analyzes the apparition, recognizing it as a projection of his own most repressed and ugly traits.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 65, 10, 'From that angle you could even be interesting to me, if I had time to bother with you...”', 'He concedes that analyzing this dark reflection could be stimulating if he weren\'t otherwise preoccupied.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 66, 11, '“I beg your pardon, I’m going to catch you now: earlier, under the street-lamp, when you jumped on Alyosha and shouted: ‘You learned it from him!', 'The visitor interrupts to expose a flaw in Ivan\'s logic, referencing a recent altercation Ivan had with his brother.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 67, 11, 'How do you know that he has been coming to me?’', 'The visitor quotes Ivan\'s own paranoid words to Alyosha, which implied Ivan believed the devil was a real entity visiting him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 68, 11, 'You were thinking of me then.', 'The apparition points out that Ivan was clearly referring to him during that outburst.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 69, 11, 'It means that for one little moment you believed, you did believe that I really am,” the gentleman laughed softly.', 'The visitor smugly concludes that Ivan\'s outburst proves he did briefly believe the devil was objectively real.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 70, 12, '“Yes, that was a lapse of character ... but I couldn’t believe in you.', 'Ivan admits to the moment of weakness but insists it did not constitute genuine belief.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 71, 12, 'I don’t know whether I was asleep or awake the last time.', 'He reiterates his confusion regarding his state of consciousness during their previous encounter.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 72, 12, 'Perhaps I only saw you in my sleep and not in reality at all.”', 'Ivan clings to the possibility that the earlier visions were just dreams.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 73, 12, '“And why were you so severe with him today, with Alyosha, I mean?', 'The visitor abruptly changes the subject to question Ivan\'s harsh treatment of his younger brother.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 74, 12, 'He’s a dear boy; I owe him one for the elder Zosima.”', 'The apparition expresses a seemingly fond, patronizing attitude toward Alyosha, referencing a past connection involving the monk Zosima.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 75, 13, '“Shut up about Alyosha!', 'Ivan fiercely protects his brother, demanding the visitor not speak of him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 76, 13, 'How dare you, you lackey!” Ivan laughed again.', 'He insults the hallucination to reassert dominance, using laughter as a defense.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 77, 14, '“You laugh while you’re abusing me—a good sign.', 'The visitor interprets Ivan\'s laughter as a positive shift away from pure anger.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 78, 14, 'By the way, you’re much more amiable with me today than you were last time, and I know why: that great decision...”', 'The apparition notes Ivan\'s comparatively better mood and attributes it to a significant recent choice Ivan has made.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 79, 15, '“Shut up about my decision!” Ivan cried ferociously.', 'Ivan is intensely triggered by the mention of his secret resolution, reacting with violent anger.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 80, 16, '“I understand, I understand, c’est noble, c’est charmant, you go to defend your brother tomorrow, and you sacrifice yourself ... c’est chevaleresque.”305', 'The visitor mockingly praises Ivan\'s plan to sacrifice his own reputation in court to save his brother.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 81, 17, '“Shut up or I’ll kick you!”', 'Driven to the edge, Ivan threatens the hallucination with physical violence.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 82, 18, '“I’d be glad of it in a way, because my goal would then be achieved: if it comes to kicks, that means you must believe in my realism, because one doesn’t kick a ghost.', 'The visitor cleverly twists the threat, explaining that a physical attack would prove Ivan accepts him as real.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 83, 18, 'Joking aside: it’s all the same to me, abuse me if you like, but still it would be better to be a bit more polite, even with me.', 'Dropping the teasing tone, the apparition asks for basic courtesy despite the abuse.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 84, 18, 'Fool, lackey— what sort of talk is that?”', 'The visitor complains that Ivan\'s insults are beneath the dignity of their conversation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 85, 19, '“By abusing you, I’m abusing myself!” Ivan laughed again.', 'Ivan laughs at the absurdity, recognizing that his insults to the visitor are ultimately self-directed.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 86, 19, '“You are me, myself, only with a different mug.', 'He reiterates that the apparition is fundamentally his own consciousness wearing a different face.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 87, 19, 'You precisely say what I already think ... and you’re not capable of telling me anything new!”', 'Ivan dismisses the entity\'s input, stating it can only parrot his pre-existing thoughts.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 88, 20, '“If my thoughts agree with yours, it only does me honor,” the gentleman said with dignity and tact.', 'The apparition gracefully accepts Ivan\'s claim, turning the idea of a shared mind into a compliment.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 89, 21, '“You just pick out all my bad thoughts, and above all the stupid ones.', 'Ivan accuses his hallucination of selectively manifesting his most foolish ideas.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 90, 21, 'You are stupid and banal.', 'He directly insults the entity\'s lack of originality.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 91, 21, 'You are terribly stupid.', 'Ivan emphasizes his profound disdain for the apparition\'s intellect.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 92, 21, 'No, I can’t endure you!', 'He expresses his overwhelming inability to tolerate the visitor\'s presence.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 93, 21, 'What am I to do, what am I to do!” Ivan gnashed his teeth.', 'Ivan grinds his teeth in sheer frustration over his inescapable torment.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 94, 22, '“My friend, I still want to be a gentleman, and to be accepted as such,” the visitor began in a fit of some sort of purely spongerish, good-natured, and already-yielding ambition.', 'The hallucination adopts the polite tone of a social parasite, requesting to be treated with respect.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 95, 22, '“I am poor, but ... I won’t say very honest, but ... in society it is generally accepted as an axiom that I am a fallen angel.', 'The visitor humorously intertwines the trope of a poor gentleman with his identity as the devil.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 96, 22, 'By God, I can’t imagine how I could ever have been an angel.', 'He ironically swears by God while expressing disbelief that he ever possessed angelic purity.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 97, 22, 'If I ever was one, it was so long ago that it’s no sin to have forgotten it.', 'He dismisses his divine past as ancient history acceptable to forget.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 98, 22, 'Now I only value my reputation as a decent man and get along as best I can, trying to be agreeable.', 'The devil claims his current goals are modest: maintaining social standing and making life pleasant.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 99, 22, 'I sincerely love people—oh, so much of what has been said about me is slander!', 'He protests that humanity has fundamentally misunderstood him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 100, 22, 'Here, when I move in with people from time to time, my life gets to be somewhat real, as it were, and I like that most of all.', 'The visitor admits that taking on human form gives him a comforting illusion of actual existence.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 101, 22, 'Because, like you, I myself suffer from the fantastic, and that is why I love your earthly realism.', 'Drawing a parallel between them, he claims he also struggles with abstract unreality.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 102, 22, 'Here you have it all outlined, here you have the formula, here you have geometry, and with us it’s all indeterminate equations!', 'He contrasts the strict physical laws of the mortal world with the chaotic nature of his spiritual realm.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 103, 22, 'I walk about here and dream.', 'The human world acts as a space where he can wander and indulge in simple fantasies.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 104, 22, 'I love to dream.', 'He emphasizes his fondness for the escape that dreaming provides.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 105, 22, 'Besides, on earth I become superstitious—don’t laugh, please: that is precisely what I like, that I become superstitious.', 'He begs Ivan not to mock him for adopting endearing human irrationalities.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 106, 22, 'Here I take on all your habits: I’ve come to love going to the public baths, can you imagine that?', 'The devil highlights his immersion in human culture by claiming a fondness for bathhouses.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 107, 22, 'I love having a steam bath with merchants and priests.', 'He enjoys the egalitarian nature of sweating alongside everyday people.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 108, 22, 'My dream is to become incarnate, but so that it’s final, irrevocable, in some fat, two-hundred-and-fifty-pound merchant’s wife, and to believe everything she believes.', 'His ultimate desire is to permanently bind himself to a simple, unquestioning human existence.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 109, 22, 'My ideal is to go into a church and light a candle with a pure heart—by God, it’s true.', 'He longs for the ability to perform an act of simple religious devotion.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 110, 22, 'That would put an end to my sufferings.', 'Such an act of innocent faith would finally relieve him of his cosmic angst.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 111, 22, 'I’ve also come to love getting medical treatment here: there was smallpox going around this spring, so I went to the foundling hospital and had myself inoculated against smallpox—if only you knew how pleased I was that day: I donated ten roubles for our brother Slavs ... !306', 'He boastfully shares his enjoyment of participating in human civic duties and charities.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 112, 22, 'But you’re not listening.', 'The visitor notices that Ivan is ignoring his monologue.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 113, 22, 'You know, you seem rather out of sorts tonight,” the gentleman paused for a moment.', 'He pauses to observe Ivan\'s poor physical and mental state.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 114, 22, '“I know you went to see that doctor yesterday ... well, how is your health?', 'Feigning concern, he asks Ivan about his medical consultation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 115, 22, 'What did the doctor say?”', 'He presses Ivan for the doctor\'s diagnosis.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 116, 23, '“Fool!”snapped Ivan.', 'Ivan forcefully interrupts the visitor\'s rambling with a single insult.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 117, 24, '“And aren’t you a smart one!', 'The visitor sarcastically praises Ivan\'s intelligence in response to the insult.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 118, 24, 'So you’re abusing me again?', 'He mildly complains that Ivan has returned to verbal attacks.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 119, 24, 'I’m just asking, not really out of sympathy.', 'He clarifies that his question about Ivan\'s health was merely conversational, not born of true care.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 120, 24, 'You don’t have to answer.', 'He permits Ivan to keep his medical details private.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 121, 24, 'And now this rheumatism’s come back ...”', 'The visitor casually pivots the conversation to his own imagined physical ailments.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 122, 25, '“Fool,” Ivan repeated.', 'Ivan dismisses the entity\'s absurd claim of having a physical illness by repeating his insult.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 123, 26, '“You keep saying the same thing, but I caught such rheumatism last year that I still remember it.”', 'The visitor chides Ivan for his repetitive insults and insists that his experience with the disease was real and memorable.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 124, 27, '“The devil with rheumatism?”', 'Ivan expresses exasperated disbelief at the paradox of a supernatural being suffering from a human joint condition.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 125, 28, '“Why not, if I sometimes become incarnate?', 'The visitor defends his claim, explaining that taking human form naturally subjects him to human frailties.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 126, 28, 'Once incarnate, I accept the consequences.', 'He asserts that he fully submits to the rules of physical existence when he embodies it.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 127, 28, 'Satan sum et nihil humanum a me alienum puto.”307', 'He humorously alters a famous Latin quote to mean \"I am Satan, and nothing human is alien to me.\"', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 128, 29, '“How’s that?', 'Ivan is caught off guard by the cleverness of the phrase.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 129, 29, 'Satan sum et nihil humanum ... not too bad for the devil!”', 'He grudgingly admits that the adapted quote is actually quite witty.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 130, 30, '“I’m glad I’ve finally pleased you.”', 'The visitor expresses satisfaction at finally winning a compliment from Ivan.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 131, 31, '“And you didn’t get that from me,” Ivan suddenly stopped as if in amazement, “that never entered my head—how strange...”', 'Ivan is bewildered, realizing that this clever thought originated from the hallucination, not from his own conscious memory.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 132, 32, '“C’est de nouveau, n’est-ce pas?308', 'The visitor proudly notes in French that he has introduced something genuinely new.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 133, 32, 'This time I’ll be honest and explain to you.', 'He offers to drop the act and provide a truthful explanation of how a hallucination can produce novel ideas.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 134, 32, 'Listen: in dreams and especially in nightmares, well, let’s say as a result of indigestion or whatever, a man sometimes sees such artistic dreams, such complex and real actuality, such events, or even a whole world of events, woven into such a plot, with such unexpected details, beginning from your highest manifestations down to the last shirt button, as I swear even Leo Tolstoy couldn’t invent; and, by the way, it’s not writers who occasionally see such dreams, but quite the most ordinary people, officials, journalists, priests. . .', 'The visitor explains the brain\'s incredible capacity to unconsciously generate highly detailed, creative, and original narratives during sleep or fever, surpassing even great novelists.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 135, 32, 'There’s even a whole problem concerning this: one government minister even confessed to me himself that all his best ideas come to him when he’s asleep.', 'He adds an anecdote about a minister to prove that the subconscious mind is often more brilliant than the conscious one.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 136, 32, 'Well, and so it is now.', 'He applies this psychological phenomenon directly to Ivan\'s current situation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 137, 32, 'Though I am your hallucination, even so, as in a nightmare, I say original things, such as have never entered your head before, so that I’m not repeating your thoughts at all, and yet I am merely your nightmare and nothing more.”', 'The visitor calmly admits he is just a dream, explaining that his apparent originality is merely Ivan\'s subconscious working at a highly creative, feverish level.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 138, 33, '“Lies.', 'Ivan immediately rejects the visitor\'s logical explanation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 139, 33, 'Your goal is precisely to convince me that you are in yourself and are not my nightmare, and so now you yourself assert that you’re a dream.”', 'Ivan suspects a trap, pointing out the psychological paradox of a hallucination deliberately claiming to be a hallucination in order to trick the host into believing it\'s real.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 140, 34, '“My friend, today I’ve adopted a special method, I’ll explain it to you later.', 'The visitor hints at a manipulative psychological tactic he is using on Ivan, promising to reveal it eventually.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 141, 34, 'Wait, where was I?', 'He casually interrupts himself, pretending to lose his train of thought.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 142, 34, 'Oh, yes, so I caught a cold, only not here, but there ...”', 'He resumes his absurd story about catching a physical illness in a metaphysical realm.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 143, 35, '“There where?', 'Ivan demands clarification on the location the visitor is referring to.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 144, 35, 'Tell me, are you going to stay long, couldn’t you go away?” Ivan exclaimed almost in despair.', 'Exhausted, Ivan pleads with the hallucination to tell him its duration and begs it to leave.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 145, 35, 'He stopped pacing, sat down on the sofa, rested his elbows on the table again, and clutched his head with both hands.', 'Overwhelmed by his illness, Ivan physically collapses into a posture of defeat.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 146, 35, 'He tore the wet towel off and threw it aside in vexation: obviously it did not help.', 'Frustrated by the failure of his practical remedy, he discards the cold compress.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 147, 36, '“Your nerves are unstrung,” the gentleman remarked, with a casually familiar and yet perfectly amiable air, “you’re angry with me even for the fact that I could catch cold, whereas it happened in the most natural way.', 'The visitor patronizingly comments on Ivan\'s anxiety, defending his absurd story as perfectly logical.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 148, 36, 'I was then hurrying to a diplomatic soirée at the home of a most highly placed Petersburg lady, who had designs on a ministry.', 'He spins a comical tale of rushing to a high-society political party.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 149, 36, 'Well, evening dress, white tie, gloves—and yet I was God knows where, and to get to your earth I still had to fly through space ... of course it only takes a moment, but then a sun’s ray takes a full eight minutes, and, imagine, in a dinner jacket, with an open vest.', 'He describes the ridiculous image of commuting through the freezing vacuum of outer space while dressed in formal human evening wear.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 150, 36, 'Spirits don’t freeze, but when one’s incarnate, then ... in short, it was flighty of me, I just set out, and in those spaces, I mean, the ether, the waters above the firmament,309 it’s so freezing cold ... that is, don’t talk about freezing— you can’t call it freezing anymore, just imagine: a hundred and fifty degrees below zero!', 'He elaborates on the cosmic cold of space, explaining that his incarnate form made him vulnerable to the extreme temperatures.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 151, 36, 'You know how village girls amuse themselves: they ask some unsuspecting novice to lick an axe at thirty degrees below zero; the tongue instantly sticks to it, and the dolt has to tear it away so that it bleeds; and that’s just at thirty below, but at a hundred and fifty, I suppose, if you just touched your finger to an axe, there would be no more finger, that is ... that is, if there happened to be an axe ...”', 'He uses a gruesome rural anecdote about freezing metal to illustrate how unfathomably cold deep space is, trailing off on the hypothetical presence of an axe in space.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 152, 37, '“And could there happen to be an axe?” Ivan Fyodorovich suddenly interrupted, absently and disgustedly.', 'Ivan is distracted by the bizarre logic of the visitor\'s analogy and interrupts him with a trivial question.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 153, 37, 'He was trying with all his might not to believe in his delirium and not to fall into complete insanity.', 'Ivan is desperately clinging to rationality, fighting against the pull of his own complex hallucinations.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 154, 38, '“An axe?” the visitor repeated in surprise.', 'The apparition acts taken aback by Ivan\'s hyper-focus on this minor detail.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 155, 39, '“Yes, what would an axe be doing there?” Ivan Fyodorovich cried with a sort of fierce and persistent stubbornness.', 'Ivan aggressively interrogates the logic of the story, using the absurdity of a cosmic axe as an anchor to prove the visitor is not real.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 156, 40, '“What would an axe be doing in space?', 'The visitor echoes the question, feigning philosophical consideration.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 157, 40, 'Quelle idée!', 'He expresses amusement in French at the strangeness of the concept.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 158, 40, 'If it got far enough away, I suppose it would begin flying around the earth, without knowing why, like a satellite.', 'The devil scientifically reasons that an axe in space would simply enter orbit due to gravity.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 159, 40, 'The astronomers would calculate the rising and setting of the axe, Gattsuk would introduce it into the calendar,310 and that’s all.”', 'He jokes that human science and society would mundanely normalize the orbiting axe by tracking its movements in common almanacs.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 160, 41, '“You are stupid, you are terribly stupid!” Ivan said cantankerously.', 'Ivan angrily insults the hallucination again, frustrated by its logical yet absurd answers.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 161, 41, '“Put more intelligence into your lies, or I won’t listen.', 'He demands higher quality intellectual stimulation if he is to be subjected to these delusions.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 162, 41, 'You want to overcome me with realism, to convince me that you are, but I don’t want to believe that you are!', 'Ivan accuses the apparition of using mundanity and logic to trick him into belief, stubbornly declaring his refusal to succumb.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 163, 41, 'I won’t believe it!!”', 'He vehemently rejects the reality of the devil.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 164, 42, '“But I’m not lying, it’s all true; unfortunately, the truth is hardly ever witty.', 'The visitor calmly states that reality is often banal, excusing his lack of grand intelligence.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 165, 42, 'You, I can see, are decidedly expecting something great from me, and perhaps even beautiful.311', 'He perceives that Ivan\'s romanticism expected a majestic, terrifying devil rather than a mundane moocher.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 166, 42, 'That’s a pity, because I give only what I can...”', 'He apologizes for disappointing Ivan, claiming he can only present himself as he actually is.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 167, 43, '“Stop philosophizing, you ass!”', 'Ivan demands the visitor cease his deep reflections and resorts to name-calling.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 168, 44, '“How philosophize, when my whole right side was numb, and I was moaning and groaning.', 'The visitor deflects the insult by returning to his pathetic story of catching a cosmic cold.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 169, 44, 'I called on the entire medical profession: they diagnose beautifully, they tell you all that’s wrong with you one-two-three, but they can’t cure you.', 'He complains about the incompetence of human doctors, who can identify but not fix illnesses.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 170, 44, 'There happened to be one enthusiastic little student: even if you die, he said, at least you’ll have a thorough knowledge of what disease you died of!', 'He mocks the cold, clinical enthusiasm of medical academia.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 171, 44, 'Then, too, they have this way of sending you to specialists: we will give you our diagnosis, they say, then go to such and such a specialist and he will cure you.', 'He critiques the modern fragmentation of medicine, where general practitioners pass patients off to narrowly focused experts.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 172, 44, 'I tell you, the old-fashioned doctor who treated all diseases has completely disappeared, now there are only specialists, and they advertise all the time in the newspapers.', 'He laments the loss of comprehensive healers in favor of commercialized specialists.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 173, 44, 'If your nose hurts, they send you to Paris: there’s a European specialist there, he treats noses.', 'He provides a hyperbolic example of the extreme geographic lengths one must go to for specific care.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 174, 44, 'You go to Paris, he examines your nose: I can treat only your right nostril, he says, I don’t treat left nostrils, it’s not my specialty, but after me, go to Vienna, there’s a separate specialist there who will finish treating your left nostril.', 'He satirizes medical hyper-specialization with a joke about doctors who only treat half a nose.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 175, 44, 'What is one to do?', 'He asks a rhetorical question about how to navigate this absurd system.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 176, 44, 'I resorted to folk remedies, one German doctor advised me to take a steam bath and rub myself with honey and salt.', 'He explains his shift to alternative, traditional medicine to cure his cosmic ailment.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 177, 44, 'I did it, only for the chance of having an extra bath: I got myself all sticky, and to no avail.', 'The remedy failed, serving only as an excuse to indulge in his love for bathing.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 178, 44, 'In desperation I wrote to Count Mattei in Milan; he sent me a book and some drops, God help him.', 'He tried another famous quack remedy out of sheer desperation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 179, 44, 'And imagine, what cured me was Hoff ‘s extract of malt!', 'He ironically claims that a commonplace commercial tonic is what finally healed him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 180, 44, 'I accidentally bought some, drank a glass and a half, and could even have danced—everything went away.', 'The simple malt drink acted as a miraculous cure for his supernatural rheumatism.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 181, 44, 'I was absolutely determined to thank him publicly in the newspapers, the feeling of gratitude was crying out in me, but, imagine, that led to another story: not one publisher would take it!', 'He shares an anecdote about trying to publish a testimonial, which was universally rejected by the press.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 182, 44, '‘It would be too retrograde, no one will believe it, le diable n’existe point.’312', 'The publishers refused because acknowledging the devil\'s existence was considered backward and unscientific.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 183, 44, 'They advised me to publish it anonymously.', 'The newspapers suggested he hide his identity to get the endorsement printed.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 184, 44, 'Well, what good is a ‘thank you’ if it’s anonymous?', 'He points out that an anonymous expression of gratitude defeats the purpose.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 185, 44, 'I had a laugh with the clerks: ‘In our day,’ I said, ‘what’s retrograde is believing in God; but I am the devil, it’s all right to believe in me. ‘', 'He shares a cynical joke he made to the publishers, highlighting modern society\'s willingness to accept evil while rejecting divinity.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 186, 44, '‘We understand,’ they said, ‘who doesn’t believe in the devil?', 'The clerks agreed with his cynical assessment of modern secularism.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 187, 44, 'But all the same we can’t do it, it might harm our tendency.', 'Despite agreeing, the publishers prioritized their progressive political reputation over printing his letter.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 188, 44, 'Or perhaps only as a joke?’', 'They offered to print it solely as a satirical piece.', '2026-07-18 15:50:08', '2026-07-18 15:50:08');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 189, 44, 'Well, I thought, as a joke it wouldn’t be very witty.', 'He rejected the offer, feeling that presenting his gratitude as a joke lacked humor.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 190, 44, 'So they simply didn’t publish it.', 'Consequently, his endorsement of the malt extract never saw print.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 191, 44, 'And would you believe that it still weighs on my heart?', 'He claims to feel genuine emotional distress over his inability to show gratitude.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 192, 44, 'My best feelings, gratitude, for example, are formally forbidden solely because of my social position.”', 'He pities himself, arguing that his role as the devil unfairly prevents him from expressing positive emotions.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 193, 45, '“Up to his neck in philosophy again!” Ivan snarled hatefully.', 'Ivan is disgusted that the visitor has once again steered a mundane story into a philosophical grievance.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 194, 46, '“God preserve me from that, but one can’t help complaining sometimes.', 'The visitor denies attempting philosophy, framing his words merely as personal venting.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 195, 46, 'I am a slandered man.', 'He insists he is the victim of cosmic misrepresentation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 196, 46, 'Even you tell me I’m stupid every other minute.', 'He uses Ivan\'s constant insults as proof of his unfair treatment.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 197, 46, 'It shows how young you are.', 'He dismisses Ivan\'s insults as the arrogance of youth.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 198, 46, 'My friend, the point is not just intelligence!', 'He argues that intellectual prowess isn\'t the only measure of a being\'s worth.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 199, 46, 'I have a naturally kind and cheerful heart,’and various little vaudevilles, I, too . . .’', 'He claims to possess a good-natured soul and an appreciation for light entertainment, quoting literature.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 200, 46, 'You seem to take me decidedly for some gray-haired Khlestakov,313 and yet my fate is far more serious.', 'He protests being viewed as a mere comedic fraud, insisting his cosmic role is deeply tragic.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 201, 46, 'By some pre-temporal assignment, which I have never been able to figure out, I am appointed ‘to negate,’ whereas I am sincerely kind and totally unable to negate.', 'He claims he was forced into the role of the ultimate adversary before time began, despite his fundamentally positive nature.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 202, 46, 'No, they say, go and negate, without negation there will be no criticism, and what sort of journal has no ‘criticism section’?', 'He uses a publishing metaphor to explain that the universe requires his evil to provide contrast and critique.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 203, 46, 'Without criticism, there would be nothing but ‘Hosannah.’', 'He points out that without a devil, the universe would be an endless, static chorus of praise.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 204, 46, 'But ‘Hosannah’ alone is not enough for life, it is necessary that this ‘Hosannah’ pass through the crucible of doubt, and so on, in the same vein.', 'He articulates the theological idea that true faith and life require the presence of doubt and adversity to be meaningful.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 205, 46, 'I don’t meddle with any of that, by the way, I didn’t create it, and I can’t answer for it.', 'He washes his hands of the universe\'s design, claiming he is merely a pawn in a system he didn\'t invent.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 206, 46, 'So they chose themselves a scapegoat, they made me write for the criticism section, and life came about.', 'He frames his existence as a cosmic scapegoat necessary for life\'s progression.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 207, 46, 'We understand this comedy: I, for instance, demand simply and directly that I be destroyed.', 'He reveals that he frequently asks for his own annihilation to escape this forced role.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 208, 46, 'No, they say, live, because without you there would be nothing.', 'He is denied destruction because his adversarial presence is structurally necessary for existence.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 209, 46, 'If everything on earth were sensible, nothing would happen.', 'He asserts that perfect rationality would result in complete stagnation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 210, 46, 'Without you there would be no events, and there must be events.', 'Chaos and evil are the catalysts that drive history and human action.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 211, 46, 'And so I serve grudgingly, for the sake of events, and I do the unreasonable on orders.', 'He portrays himself as a reluctant public servant executing divine commands to cause trouble.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 212, 46, 'People take this whole comedy for something serious, despite all their undeniable intelligence.', 'He mocks humanity for treating the cosmic game of good and evil with such heavy seriousness.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 213, 46, 'That is their tragedy.', 'He pities humans for their inability to see the absurdity of the universe.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 214, 46, 'Well, they suffer, of course, but ... still they live, they live really, not in fantasy; for suffering is life.', 'He defines human existence by its capacity for suffering, contrasting it with his own empty state.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 215, 46, 'Without suffering, what pleasure would there be in it—everything would turn into an endless prayer service: holy, but a bit dull.', 'He argues that paradise without pain would be unbearably monotonous.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 216, 46, 'And me?', 'He pivots to wallowing in his own existential misery.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 217, 46, 'I suffer, and still I do not live.', 'Unlike humans, his suffering brings him no true sense of vital existence.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 218, 46, 'I am an x in an indeterminate equation.', 'He describes himself as an unresolved, abstract necessity rather than a real entity.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 219, 46, 'I am some sort of ghost of life who has lost all ends and beginnings, and I’ve finally even forgotten what to call myself.', 'He expresses profound identity loss, reduced to a mere shadow of being.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 220, 46, 'You’re laughing ... no, you’re not laughing, you’re angry again.', 'He tries to read Ivan\'s reaction, misinterpreting his silent rage.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 221, 46, 'You’re eternally angry, you want reason only, but I will repeat to you once more that I would give all of that life beyond the stars, all ranks and honors, only to be incarnated in the soul of a two-hundred-and-fifty-pound merchant’s wife and light candles to God.”', 'He chides Ivan\'s obsession with logic and repeats his desperate wish to trade his cosmic status for simple, ignorant human faith.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 222, 47, '“So you don’t believe in God, then?” Ivan grinned hatefully.', 'Ivan seizes on the devil\'s theological rambling to aggressively interrogate him about his actual belief in a creator.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 223, 48, '“Well, how shall I put it—that is, if you’re serious...”', 'The visitor stalls, surprised by the direct theological question.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 224, 49, '“Is there a God, or not?” Ivan cried again with fierce insistence.', 'Ivan demands a clear, definitive answer about the existence of God.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 225, 50, '“Ah, so you are serious?', 'The visitor acknowledges Ivan\'s earnest desperation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 226, 50, 'By God, my dear, I just don’t know—there’s a great answer for you!”', 'The devil absurdly admits he is genuinely agnostic about God\'s existence, failing to provide Ivan the certainty he craves.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 227, 51, '“You don’t know, yet you see God?', 'Ivan points out the contradiction of a spiritual being doubting the creator it supposedly interacts with.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 228, 51, 'No, you are not in yourself, you are me, me and nothing else!', 'Ivan uses this paradoxical answer as proof that the devil is merely a reflection of Ivan\'s own agnostic mind.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 229, 51, 'You are trash, you are my fantasy!”', 'He denigrates the apparition, reasserting his belief that it is an illusion.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 230, 52, '“Let’s say I’m of one philosophy with you, if you like, that would be correct.', 'The visitor agrees that his worldview aligns perfectly with Ivan\'s.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 231, 52, 'Je pense donc je suis,314 I’m quite sure of that, but all the rest around me, all those worlds, God, even Satan himself—for me all that is unproven, whether it exists in itself, or is only my emanation, a consistent development of my I, which exists pre-temporally and uniquely ... in short, I hasten to stop, because you look as if you’re about to jump up and start fighting.”', 'The devil adopts a solipsistic philosophy, declaring certainty only of his own mind while doubting the reality of everything else, but cuts himself off when he sees Ivan\'s violent fury.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 232, 53, '“Better tell me some funny anecdote!” Ivan said sickly.', 'Physically exhausted by the philosophical torment, Ivan begs for a distracting story.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 233, 54, '“There is an anecdote, and precisely on our subject—that is, not an anecdote but more of a legend.', 'The visitor obliges, preparing to tell a tale relevant to their discussion of faith and suffering.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 234, 54, 'You reproach me with unbelief: ‘You see, but you don’t believe.’', 'He references Ivan\'s earlier criticism of his agnosticism.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 235, 54, 'But, my friend, I am not alone in that, all of us there are stirred up now, and it all comes from your science.', 'He claims that spiritual entities are also suffering crises of faith, driven by humanity\'s scientific discoveries.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 236, 54, 'While there were still just atoms, five senses, four elements, well, then it all still stayed together anyhow.', 'He notes that ancient, simpler science was compatible with their spiritual worldview.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 237, 54, 'They had atoms in the ancient world, too.', 'He acknowledges early atomic theory.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 238, 54, 'But when we found out that you had discovered your ‘chemical molecule,’ and ‘protoplasm,’ and devil knows what else—then we put our tails between our legs.', 'He humorously admits that modern biology and chemistry deeply intimidated and confused the spiritual realm.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 239, 54, 'A real muddle set in; above all—superstition, gossip we have as much gossip as you do, even a bit more; and, finally, denunciations as well we, too, have a certain department where such ‘information’ is received .315', 'The scientific revolution caused chaos, paranoia, and a bureaucracy of informants in hell.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 240, 54, 'And so there is this wild legend, which goes back to our middle ages—not yours but ours—and no one believes it except for two-hundred-and-fifty-pound merchants’ wives—that is, again, not your merchants’ wives but ours.', 'He introduces a myth from hell\'s own history, noting it\'s only believed by the most gullible among them.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 241, 54, 'Everything that you have, we have as well; I’m revealing one of our secrets to you, out of friendship, though it’s forbidden.', 'He confides that hell mirrors human society, breaking supernatural rules to share this detail.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 242, 54, 'This legend is about paradise.', 'He states the subject of the upcoming tale.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 243, 54, 'There was, they say, a certain thinker and philosopher here on your earth, who ‘rejected all—laws, conscience, faith,’316 and, above all, the future life.', 'The story centers on an absolute atheist who denied everything, especially the afterlife.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 244, 54, 'He died and thought he’d go straight into darkness and death, but no—there was the future life before him.', 'Upon dying, the atheist was shocked to find that the afterlife was real.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 245, 54, 'He was amazed and indignant: ‘This,’ he said, ‘goes against my convictions.’', 'The philosopher hilariously protested the existence of the afterlife on the grounds of his personal beliefs.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 246, 54, 'So for that he was sentenced ... I mean, you see, I beg your pardon, I’m repeating what I heard, it’s just a legend ... you see, he was sentenced to walk in darkness a quadrillion kilometers we also use kilometers now, and once he finished that quadrillion, the doors of paradise would be opened to him and he would be forgiven everything.”', 'For his obstinate denial, he was condemned to walk an astronomical distance in the dark, with the promise of paradise and forgiveness upon completion.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 247, 55, '“And what other torments have you got in that world, besides the quadrillion?” Ivan interrupted with some strange animation.', 'Ivan suddenly becomes highly interested and asks about the specific punishments in hell.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 248, 56, '“What other torments?', 'The visitor repeats the question.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 249, 56, 'Ah, don’t even ask: before it was one thing and another, but now it’s mostly the moral sort, ‘remorse of conscience’ and all that nonsense.', 'He complains that hell has shifted away from physical torture to psychological and moral suffering.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 250, 56, 'That also started because of you, from the ‘mellowing of your mores.’317', 'He blames this shift on humanity\'s increasing modern sensitivity and humanism.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 251, 56, 'Well, and who benefited?', 'He questions the effectiveness of this progressive reform in hell.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 252, 56, 'The unscrupulous benefited, because what is remorse of conscience to a man who has no conscience at all?', 'He points out the flaw: moral torture doesn\'t work on truly evil people.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 253, 56, 'Decent people who still had some conscience and honor left suffered instead ...', 'Ironically, only the slightly flawed people capable of guilt are actually punished by this system.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 254, 56, 'There you have it—reforms on unprepared ground, and copied from foreign institutions as well—nothing but harm!', 'He satirizes Russian political reforms by comparing them to hell\'s failed administrative changes.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 255, 56, 'The good old fire was much better.', 'He nostalgically prefers the simplicity of physical hellfire.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 256, 56, 'Well, so this man sentenced to the quadrillion stood a while, looked, and then lay down across the road: ‘I don’t want to go, I refuse to go on principle! ‘', 'Returning to the story, he describes how the stubborn philosopher laid down in the dark and refused his punishment out of sheer pride.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 257, 56, 'Take the soul of an enlightened Russian atheist and mix it with the soul of the prophet Jonah, who sulked in the belly of a whale for three days and three nights—you’ll get the character of this thinker lying in the road.”', 'He compares the philosopher\'s stubborn, sulking nature to a mix of modern nihilism and biblical obstinacy.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 258, 57, '“And what was he lying on?”', 'Ivan interrupts to ask a pedantic question about the physical reality of the punishment.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 259, 57, '“Well, there must have been something there.', 'The visitor guesses vaguely at the nature of the ground.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 260, 57, 'Or are you laughing?”', 'He notices Ivan\'s strange reaction.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 261, 58, '“Bravo!” cried Ivan, still with the same strange animation.', 'Ivan excitedly applauds the story.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 262, 58, 'He was listening now with unexpected curiosity.', 'The narrator notes Ivan\'s intense engagement with the narrative.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 263, 58, '“Well, so is he still lying there?”', 'Ivan asks for the resolution of the philosopher\'s protest.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 264, 59, '“The point is that he isn’t.', 'The devil reveals the man eventually gave up his protest.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 265, 59, 'He lay there for nearly a thousand years, and then got up and started walking.”', 'After an immense period of stubbornness, the philosopher finally began his trek.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 266, 60, '“What an ass!” Ivan exclaimed, bursting into nervous laughter, still apparently trying hard to figure something out.', 'Ivan mocks the philosopher\'s futile protest, laughing nervously as his brain struggles with a sudden realization.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 267, 60, '“Isn’t it all the same whether he lies there forever or walks a quadrillion kilometers?', 'Ivan points out the mathematical futility of the task.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 268, 60, 'It must be about a billion years’ walk!”', 'He estimates the immense time required to complete the journey.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 269, 61, '“Much more, even.', 'The visitor agrees that the timeframe is unfathomably huge.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 270, 61, 'If we had a pencil and paper, we could work it out.', 'He casually suggests doing the math.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 271, 61, 'But he arrived long ago, and this is where the anecdote begins.”', 'He reveals that the journey is already over, setting up the punchline.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 272, 62, '“Arrived!', 'Ivan is shocked by this temporal impossibility.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 273, 62, 'But where did he get a billion years?”', 'He questions how such an immense amount of time could have already passed.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 274, 63, '“You keep thinking about our present earth!', 'The visitor chides Ivan for his limited, linear view of time.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 275, 63, 'But our present earth may have repeated itself a billion times; it died out, let’s say, got covered with ice, cracked, fell to pieces, broke down into its original components, again there were the waters above the firmament, then again a comet, again the sun, again the earth from the sun—all this development may already have been repeated an infinite number of times, and always in the same way, to the last detail.', 'He explains a cyclical view of the universe, where history destroys and repeats itself identically over eons, allowing for billions of years to pass.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 276, 63, 'A most unspeakable bore...”', 'He expresses his eternal exhaustion with this repetitive cosmic cycle.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 277, 64, '“Go on, what happened when he arrived?”', 'Ivan impatiently demands the end of the story.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 278, 65, '“The moment the doors of paradise were opened and he went in, before he had even been there two seconds—and that by the watch, the watch though I should think that on the way his watch would long ago have broken down into its component elements in his pocket—before he had been there two seconds, he exclaimed that for those two seconds it would be worth walking not just a quadrillion kilometers, but a quadrillion quadrillion, even raised to the quadrillionth power!', 'The visitor describes how the atheist, upon experiencing heaven for mere seconds, declared the ecstasy was worth infinitely more suffering than he had endured.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 279, 65, 'In short, he sang ‘Hosannah’ and oversweetened it so much that some persons there, of a nobler cast of mind, did not even want to shake hands with him at first: he jumped over to the conservatives a bit too precipitously.', 'The philosopher\'s immediate and overly enthusiastic conversion to faith disgusted the more stoic, established members of paradise.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 280, 65, 'The Russian character.', 'The visitor attributes this extreme, rapid ideological swing to Russian nature.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 281, 65, 'I repeat: it’s a legend.', 'He reminds Ivan of the story\'s fictional status within his realm.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 282, 65, 'Take it for what it’s worth.', 'He invites Ivan to draw his own conclusions.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 283, 65, 'That’s the sort of ideas current among us on all these subjects.”', 'He concludes that this tale represents the theological gossip of hell.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 284, 66, '“Caught you!” Ivan cried out with almost childish glee, as if he had now finally remembered something.', 'Ivan triumphantly realizes why the story sounded familiar, experiencing a moment of victorious clarity.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 285, 66, '“That anecdote about the quadrillion years— I made it up myself!', 'He reveals that the entire story is his own original composition.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 286, 66, 'I was seventeen years old then, I was in high school ... I made up that anecdote then and told it to a friend of mine, his last name was Korovkin, it was in Moscow ...', 'He precisely recalls the context of inventing the story in his youth.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 287, 66, 'It’s such a typical anecdote that I couldn’t have gotten it from anywhere.', 'He asserts the unique nature of the idea proves it is his.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 288, 66, 'I almost forgot it ... but now I’ve unconsciously recalled it—recalled it myself, not because you told it to me!', 'He realizes that the hallucination narrating the story was just his own brain retrieving a repressed memory.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 289, 66, 'Just as one sometimes recalls a thousand things unconsciously, even when one is being taken out to be executed ...', 'He compares this sudden memory retrieval to a psychological phenomenon that occurs in moments of extreme stress.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 290, 66, 'I’ve remembered it in a dream.', 'He firmly classifies the experience as an internal dream state.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 291, 66, 'You are my dream!', 'He reasserts his dominance over the apparition.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 292, 66, 'You’re a dream, you don’t exist!”', 'He vehemently denies the devil\'s independent reality.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 293, 67, '“Judging by the enthusiasm with which you deny me,” the gentleman laughed, “I’m convinced that you do believe in me all the same.”', 'The visitor laughs off Ivan\'s victory, arguing that the intense passion of his denial proves a subconscious belief in the devil\'s reality.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 294, 68, '“Not in the least!', 'Ivan fiercely rejects this psychological assessment.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 295, 68, 'Not for a hundredth part do I believe in you!”', 'He attempts to quantify his absolute lack of faith in the entity.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 296, 69, '“But for a thousandth part you do believe.', 'The apparition counters that a microscopic shred of belief remains.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 297, 69, 'Homeopathic doses are perhaps the strongest.', 'He references homeopathy to suggest that the smallest trace of faith is incredibly potent.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 298, 69, 'Admit that you do believe, let’s say for a ten-thousandth part ...”', 'He tries to bargain Ivan into admitting a fractional amount of belief.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 299, 70, '“Not for one moment!” Ivan cried in a rage.', 'Ivan refuses to concede even a fraction of belief, blinded by anger.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 300, 70, '“And, by the way, I should like to believe in you!” he suddenly added strangely.', 'In a paradoxical twist, Ivan admits a deep, irrational desire for the devil—and by extension, the spiritual world—to be real.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 301, 71, '“Aha!', 'The visitor seizes on this admission triumphantly.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 302, 71, 'Quite a confession, really!', 'He highlights the immense significance of Ivan\'s vulnerability.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 303, 71, 'But I am kind, I will help you here, too.', 'He patronizingly offers to assist Ivan in his spiritual struggle.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 304, 71, 'Listen, it is I who have caught you, not you me!', 'He reverses Ivan\'s earlier victory, claiming he orchestrated the entire memory retrieval.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 305, 71, 'I deliberately told you your own anecdote, which you had forgotten, so that you would finally lose faith in me.”', 'He claims his strategy was to incite disbelief by proving he was just a manifestation of Ivan\'s memory.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 306, 72, '“Lies!', 'Ivan refuses to accept this convoluted manipulation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 307, 72, 'The purpose of your appearance is to convince me that you are.”', 'He insists that the devil\'s only goal must be to prove his own existence.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 308, 73, '“Precisely.', 'The visitor agrees with Ivan\'s premise.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 309, 73, 'But hesitation, anxiety, the struggle between belief and disbelief—all that is sometimes such a torment for a conscientious man like yourself, that it’s better to hang oneself.', 'He explains that agonizing uncertainty is far more psychologically damaging than outright disbelief.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 310, 73, 'Precisely because I knew you had a tiny bit of belief in me, I let in some final disbelief, by telling you that anecdote.', 'He explains his tactic: pushing Ivan to total disbelief to create a psychological rubber-band effect.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 311, 73, 'I’m leading you alternately between belief and disbelief, and I have my own purpose in doing so.', 'He admits to playing a calculated psychological game with Ivan\'s sanity.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 312, 73, 'A new method, sir: when you’ve completely lost faith in me, then you’ll immediately start convincing me to my face that I am not a dream but a reality—I know you now; and then my goal will be achieved.', 'He predicts that Ivan\'s contrarian nature will force him to argue for the devil\'s reality once he fully convinces himself it\'s a dream.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 313, 73, 'And it is a noble goal.', 'He ironically claims his manipulative torture has a holy purpose.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 314, 73, 'I will sow just a tiny seed of faith in you, and from it an oak will grow—and such an oak that you, sitting in that oak, will want to join ‘the desert fathers and the blameless women’;318 because secretly you want that verry, ver-ry much, you will dine on locusts, you will drag yourself to the desert to seek salvation!”', 'He prophesies that this psychological torment will eventually force Ivan to abandon his atheism, embrace extreme ascetic faith, and seek salvation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 315, 74, '“So, you scoundrel, you’re troubling yourself over the salvation of my soul?”', 'Ivan is deeply offended and incredulous that his own hallucination is trying to force him into religious salvation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 316, 75, '“One needs to do a good deed sometimes, at least.', 'The devil casually jokes about fulfilling a quota for good behavior.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 317, 75, 'But I see you’re angry with me, really angry!”', 'He notes with satisfaction that his manipulation is enraging Ivan.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 318, 76, '“Buffoon!', 'Ivan insults him again.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 319, 76, 'And have you ever tempted them, the ones who eat locusts and pray for seventeen years in the barren desert, and get overgrown with moss?”', 'Ivan challenges the devil\'s track record, asking if he has ever successfully corrupted true, extreme ascetics.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 320, 77, '“My dear, I’ve done nothing else.', 'The visitor boasts that tempting holy men is his primary occupation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 321, 77, 'One forgets the whole world and all worlds, and clings to such a one, because a diamond like that is just too precious; one such soul is sometimes worth a whole constellation—we have our own arithmetic.', 'He explains that corrupting a deeply holy ascetic is a prize valued infinitely higher than corrupting ordinary souls.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 322, 77, 'It’s a precious victory!', 'He views destroying pure faith as his greatest triumph.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 323, 77, 'And some of them, by God, are not inferior to you in development, though you won’t believe it: they can contemplate such abysses of belief and disbelief at one and the same moment that, really, it sometimes seems that another hair’s breadth and a man would fall in ‘heel-over-headed,’ as the actor Gorbunov says.”319', 'He notes that these ascetics possess immense intellectual and spiritual depth, constantly balancing on the razor\'s edge between profound faith and absolute despair.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 324, 78, '“So, what?', 'Ivan presses him for the outcome of these temptations.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 325, 78, 'They put your nose out of joint?”', 'He uses an idiom to ask if the holy men ultimately defeated the devil.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 326, 79, '“My friend,” the visitor observed sententiously, “it’s sometimes better to have your nose put out of joint than to have no nose at all, as one afflicted marquis he must have been treated by a specialist uttered not long ago in confession to his Jesuit spiritual director.', 'The devil uses a pun and a comedic anecdote about a disfigured nobleman to answer Ivan.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 327, 79, 'I was present—it was just lovely.', 'He claims to have witnessed this bizarre confession firsthand.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 328, 79, '‘Give me back my nose!’ he said, beating his breast.', 'He acts out the nobleman\'s despair over losing his nose to disease.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 329, 79, '‘My son,’ the priest hedged, ‘through the inscrutable decrees of Providence everything has its recompense, and a visible calamity sometimes brings with it a great, if invisible, profit.', 'He mimics the Jesuit priest using twisted religious logic to comfort the man.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 330, 79, 'If a harsh fate has deprived you of your nose, your profit is that now for the rest of your life no one will dare tell you that you have had your nose put out of joint.’', 'The priest absurdly suggests that literal disfigurement protects the man from metaphorical insults.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 331, 79, '‘Holy father, that’s no consolation!’ the desperate man exclaimed.', 'The nobleman rejected this ridiculous comfort.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 332, 79, '‘On the contrary, I’d be delighted to have my nose put out of joint every day of my life, if only it were where it belonged!’', 'The man preferred enduring daily insults if it meant having his physical face restored.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 333, 79, '‘My son,’ the priest sighed, ‘one cannot demand all blessings at once.', 'The priest chastised the man for wanting too much.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 334, 79, 'That is to murmur against Providence, which even here has not forgotten you; for if you cry, as you have just cried, that you would gladly have your nose put out of joint for the rest of your life, in this your desire has already been fulfilled indirectly; for, having lost your nose, you have thereby, as it were, had your nose put out of joint all the same ...”', 'The priest used absurd casuistry to argue that the man\'s suffering was actually God fulfilling his wish.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 335, 80, '“Pah, how stupid!” cried Ivan.', 'Ivan expresses disgust at the absolute absurdity and immorality of the joke.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 336, 81, '“My friend, I merely wanted to make you laugh, but I swear that is real Jesuit casuistry, and I swear it all happened word for word as I’ve told it to you.', 'The visitor insists the anecdote is historically accurate and an example of genuine theological hypocrisy.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 337, 81, 'That was a recent incident, and it gave me a lot of trouble.', 'He hints that the fallout of this event caused him logistical issues in hell.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 338, 81, 'The unfortunate young man went home and shot himself that same night; I was with him constantly up to the last moment ...', 'He reveals the dark conclusion of the story, claiming he accompanied the despairing man to his suicide.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 339, 81, 'As for those little Jesuit confessional booths, that truly is my pet amusement in the sadder moments of life.', 'The devil admits he deeply enjoys watching the corruption and hypocrisy that occurs during religious confessions.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 340, 81, 'Here’s another incident for you, from just the other day.', 'He immediately launches into a second story.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 341, 81, 'A girl comes to an old priest, a blonde, from Normandy, about twenty years old.', 'He sets the scene with a young, attractive woman.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 342, 81, 'Beautiful, buxom, all nature—enough to make your mouth water.', 'He describes her in purely physical, lustful terms.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 343, 81, 'She bends down and whispers her sin to the priest through the little hole.', 'She confesses a sexual transgression.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 344, 81, '‘What, my daughter, can you have fallen again so soon ... ?’ the priest exclaims.', 'The priest reacts with shock to her repeated sins.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 345, 81, '’O Sancta Maria, what’s this I hear?', 'The priest invokes Mary in horror.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 346, 81, 'With another man now?', 'He discovers her promiscuity.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 347, 81, 'But how long will it go on?', 'He questions her morality.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 348, 81, 'What shame! ‘', 'He attempts to shame her.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 349, 81, '‘Ah, mon père,’ the sinner replies, bathed in tears of repentance, ‘ça lui fait tant de plaisir, et à moi si peu de peine!’320', 'The girl replies in French that the act gives the men immense pleasure and costs her very little trouble, mixing genuine naivety with utter moral looseness.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 350, 81, 'Well, just imagine such an answer!', 'The devil marvels at the girl\'s shockingly pragmatic view of sin.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 351, 81, 'At that even I backed off: it was the very cry of nature, which, if you like, is better than innocence itself.', 'He claims her unashamed natural instinct was more powerful and pure than strict religious morality.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 352, 81, 'I remitted her sin on the spot and turned to leave, but I had to come back at once: I heard the priest arranging a rendezvous with her for that evening through the hole; the old man was solid as a rock, but he fell in an instant!', 'He describes how the supposedly devout priest immediately succumbed to lust and propositioned the girl.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 353, 81, 'It was nature, the truth of nature, claiming its own!', 'He attributes the priest\'s fall to the undeniable power of biological instinct over religious dogma.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 354, 81, 'What, are you turning your nose up again, are you angry again?', 'He notices Ivan\'s continued disgust.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 355, 81, 'I really don’t know how to please you . . .”', 'He pretends to be helpless in his attempts to entertain Ivan.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 356, 82, '“Leave me, you’re throbbing in my brain like a persistent nightmare,” Ivan groaned painfully, powerless before his apparition.', 'Ivan physically suffers from the hallucination, begging it to stop tormenting him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 357, 82, '“I’m bored with you, it’s unbearable, agonizing!', 'He declares the experience both tedious and deeply painful.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 358, 82, 'I’d give a lot to be able to get rid of you!”', 'He expresses desperate willingness to do anything to banish the vision.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 359, 83, '“I repeat, moderate your demands, don’t demand ‘all that is great and beautiful’321 of me, and we shall live in peace and harmony, you’ll see,” the gentleman said imposingly.', 'The devil haughtily advises Ivan to lower his expectations of reality to find peace.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 360, 83, '“Indeed, you’re angry with me that I have not appeared to you in some sort of red glow, ‘in thunder and lightning,’ with scorched wings, but have presented myself in such a modest form.', 'He accurately analyzes Ivan\'s disappointment that his personal demon is not a majestic, terrifying entity.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 361, 83, 'You’re insulted, first, in your aesthetic feelings, and, second, in your pride: how could such a banal devil come to such a great man?', 'He strikes at Ivan\'s ego, stating that Ivan feels his intellect deserves a much grander adversary.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 362, 83, 'No, you’ve still got that romantic little streak in you, so derided by Belinsky.322', 'He mocks Ivan\'s outdated, romantic worldview, referencing a famous Russian literary critic.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 363, 83, 'It can’t be helped, young man.', 'He condescendingly dismisses Ivan\'s youthful idealism.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 364, 83, 'This evening, as I was getting ready to come to you, I did think of appearing, for a joke, in the form of a retired Regular State Councillor who had served in the Caucasus, with the star of the Lion and Sun pinned to my frock coat, but I was decidedly afraid, because you’d have thrashed me just for daring to tack the Lion and Sun on my frock coat, instead of the North Star or Sirius at least.323', 'He jokes that he considered appearing as a decorated bureaucrat, but knew Ivan\'s cosmic arrogance would demand nothing less than a star from the cosmos itself.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 365, 83, 'And you keep saying how stupid I am.', 'He addresses Ivan\'s constant insults to his intelligence.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 366, 83, 'But, my God, I don’t make any claims to being your equal in intelligence.', 'He falsely humbles himself before Ivan\'s intellect.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 367, 83, 'Mephistopheles, when he comes to Faust, testifies of himself that he desires evil, yet does only good.324', 'He references Goethe\'s devil, who inadvertently causes good while attempting evil.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 368, 83, 'Well, let him do as he likes, it’s quite the opposite with me.', 'He claims his own nature is the exact reverse of Mephistopheles.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 369, 83, 'I am perhaps the only man in all of nature who loves the truth and sincerely desires good.', 'He makes the astonishing claim that the devil actually yearns for goodness and truth.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 370, 83, 'I was there when the Word who died on the cross was ascending into heaven, carrying on his bosom the soul of the thief who was crucified to the right of him, I heard the joyful shrieks of the cherubim singing and shouting ‘Hosannah,’ and the thundering shout of rapture from the seraphim, which made heaven and all creation shake.', 'He describes witnessing the majestic, world-shaking resurrection and ascension of Christ.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 371, 83, 'And, I swear by all that’s holy, I wanted to join the chorus and shout ‘Hosannah’ with everyone else.', 'He claims he was profoundly moved and almost surrendered to divine worship.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 372, 83, 'It was right on my lips, it was already bursting from my breast ... you know, I’m very sensitive and artistically susceptible.', 'He blames his momentary weakness on his appreciation for grand, beautiful spectacles.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 373, 83, 'But common sense—oh, it’s the most unfortunate quality of my nature—kept me within due bounds even then, and I missed the moment!', 'He asserts that cold rationality prevented him from giving in to faith.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 374, 83, 'For what—I thought at that same moment—what will happen after my ‘Hosannah?', 'He outlines the logical calculation that stopped him.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 375, 83, 'Everything in the world will immediately be extinguished and no events will occur.', 'He reiterates that his surrender would mean the end of all conflict, and therefore the end of existence itself.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 376, 83, 'And so, solely because of my official duty and my social position, I was forced to quash the good moment in myself and stay with my nasty tricks.', 'He portrays himself as a tragic martyr to cosmic necessity, forced to do evil to keep the universe running.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 377, 83, 'Someone takes all the honor of the good for himself and only leaves me the nasty tricks.', 'He complains bitterly about God taking the glory while assigning him the dirty work.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 378, 83, 'But I don’t covet the honor of living as a moocher, I’m not ambitious.', 'He insists he doesn\'t want this role.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 379, 83, 'Why, of all beings in the world, am I alone condemned to be cursed by all decent people, and even to be kicked with boots, for, when I become incarnate, I must occasionally take such consequences as well?', 'He whines about the universal hatred and physical indignities he suffers.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 380, 83, 'There’s a secret here, I know, but they won’t reveal this secret to me for anything, because then, having learned what it’s all about, I might just roar ‘Hosannah,’ and the necessary minus would immediately disappear and sensibleness would set in all over the world, and with it, of course, the end of everything, even of newspapers and journals, because who would subscribe to them?', 'He suspects God is hiding the ultimate meaning of the universe from him, fearing that if the devil knew the truth, he would repent and accidentally destroy creation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 381, 83, 'I know that I will finally be reconciled, that I, too, will finish my quadrillion and be let in on the secret.', 'He expresses a hope for eventual cosmic reconciliation and forgiveness at the end of time.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 382, 83, 'But until that happens I sulk and grudgingly fulfill my purpose: to destroy thousands so that one may be saved.', 'Until the end of time, he bitterly performs his duty of creating adversity to forge human salvation.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 383, 83, 'For instance, how many souls had to be destroyed, and honest reputations put to shame, in order to get just one righteous Job, with whom they baited me so wickedly in olden times!', 'He complains about the massive collateral damage required by God to prove a single man\'s faith, referencing the biblical Book of Job.', '2026-07-18 15:50:09', '2026-07-18 15:50:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 384, 83, 'No, until the secret is revealed, two truths exist for me: one is theirs, from there, and so far completely unknown to me; the other is mine.', 'He declares a philosophical divide: divine truth, which is hidden, and his own cynical, worldly truth.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 385, 83, 'And who knows which is preferable ...', 'He questions which truth is actually better.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 386, 83, 'Are you asleep?”', 'He checks to see if Ivan has passed out from the rant.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 387, 84, '“What else?” Ivan groaned spitefully.', 'Ivan, still awake, dismisses the tirade with hateful exhaustion.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 388, 84, '“Everything in my nature that is stupid, long outlived, mulled over in my mind, flung away like carrion—you are now offering to me as some kind of news!”', 'Ivan accuses the hallucination of merely regurgitating Ivan\'s own discarded, adolescent philosophies as if they were profound revelations.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 389, 85, '“Displeased again!', 'The visitor acts offended by Ivan\'s critique.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 390, 85, 'And I hoped you might even be charmed by such a literary rendition: that ‘Hosannah’ in heaven really didn’t come out too badly, did it?', 'He proudly defends the poetic quality of his storytelling.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 391, 85, 'And then that sarcastic tone, à la Heine,325 eh?', 'He boasts about adopting the cynical style of the poet Heinrich Heine.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 392, 85, 'Don’t you agree?”', 'He fishes for a compliment.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 393, 86, '“No, never have I been such a lackey!', 'Ivan furiously denies ever being as pathetic and subservient as the apparition.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 394, 86, 'How could my soul produce such a lackey as you?”', 'He is deeply disturbed that his own mind could generate such a groveling, banal entity.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 395, 87, '“My friend, I know a most charming and dear young Russian gentleman: a thinker and a great lover of literature and other fine things, the author of a promising poem entitled ‘The Grand Inquisitor’...', 'The devil slyly references Ivan himself and Ivan\'s famous, deeply personal poem.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 396, 87, 'It was him only that I had in mind.”', 'He insinuates that he modeled his persona directly on Ivan\'s own intellectual pretensions.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 397, 88, '“I forbid you to speak of ‘The Grand Inquisitor,’” Ivan exclaimed, blushing all over with shame.', 'Ivan is profoundly humiliated that his most closely guarded, serious work is being mocked by his own madness.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 398, 89, '“Well, and what about the ‘Geological Cataclysm’?', 'The visitor ignores Ivan and brings up another of Ivan\'s philosophical theories.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 399, 89, 'Remember that?', 'He taunts Ivan with his past ideas.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 400, 89, 'What a poem!”', 'He mockingly praises the concept.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 401, 90, '“Shut up, or I’ll kill you!”', 'Ivan\'s shame turns into violent, homicidal rage against the hallucination.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 402, 91, '“Kill me?', 'The visitor laughs at the impossibility of killing a spirit.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 403, 91, 'No, excuse me, but I will have my say.', 'He refuses to be silenced.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 404, 91, 'I came in order to treat myself to that pleasure.', 'He admits he manifested specifically to torture Ivan with his own words.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 405, 91, 'Oh, I love the dreams of my friends—fervent, young, trembling with the thirst for life!', 'He patronizingly praises the arrogant, ambitious ideas of young intellectuals like Ivan.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 406, 91, '‘There are new people now,’ you decided last spring, as you were preparing to come here, ‘they propose to destroy everything and begin with anthropophagy.', 'The devil begins quoting Ivan\'s own past theories about modern radicals who want to destroy society down to cannibalism.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 407, 91, 'Fools, they never asked me!', 'He quotes Ivan\'s arrogant belief that the radicals were doing it wrong.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 408, 91, 'In my opinion, there is no need to destroy anything, one need only destroy the idea of God in mankind, that’s where the business should start!', 'He repeats Ivan\'s core philosophy: humanity\'s emancipation requires only the destruction of faith, not physical structures.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 409, 91, 'One should begin with that, with that—oh, blind men, of no understanding!', 'He mimics Ivan\'s condescension toward those who didn\'t grasp this concept.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 410, 91, 'Once mankind has renounced God, one and all and I believe that this period, analogous to the geological periods, will come, then the entire old world view will fall of itself, without anthropophagy, and, above all, the entire former morality, and everything will be new.', 'He outlines Ivan\'s utopian vision: the death of God will naturally lead to a new, advanced human morality without violent destruction.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 411, 91, 'People will come together in order to take from life all that it can give, but, of course, for happiness and joy in this world only.', 'Without the afterlife, humanity will focus entirely on maximizing earthly happiness.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 412, 91, 'Man will be exalted with the spirit of divine, titanic pride, and the man-god will appear.', 'Freed from divine subservience, humanity will elevate itself to godhood.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 413, 91, 'Man, his will and his science no longer limited, conquering nature every hour, will thereby every hour experience such lofty delight as will replace for him all his former hopes of heavenly delight.', 'Technological and scientific mastery over nature will provide the transcendent joy previously sought in religion.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 414, 91, 'Each will know himself utterly mortal, without resurrection, and will accept death proudly and calmly, like a god.', 'Accepting absolute mortality will give humans a dignified, god-like stoicism.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 415, 91, 'Out of pride he will understand that he should not murmur against the momentariness of life, and he will love his brother then without any reward.', 'Without heaven as a reward, human love and brotherhood will become pure and selfless.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 416, 91, 'Love will satisfy only the moment of life, but the very awareness of its momentariness will increase its fire, inasmuch as previously it was diffused in hopes of an eternal love beyond the grave’ ... well, and so on and so on, in the same vein.', 'The fleeting nature of life will make human connections intensely passionate, contrasting with the diluted love promised by eternity.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 417, 91, 'Lovely!”', 'The devil finishes quoting Ivan\'s grand theory, calling it beautiful but ultimately hollow.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 418, 92, 'Ivan was sitting with his hands over his ears, looking down, but his whole body started trembling.', 'Unable to bear hearing his own arrogant theories mocked, Ivan physically tries to block out the sound, shaking with severe distress.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 419, 92, 'The voice went on:', 'The hallucination relentlessly continues its assault.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 420, 93, '“‘The question now,’ my young thinker reflected, ‘is whether or not it is possible for such a period ever to come.', 'The devil quotes Ivan\'s private doubts about whether this atheist utopia will ever materialize.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 421, 93, 'If it does come, then everything will be resolved and mankind will finally be settled.', 'Ivan believed this era would bring ultimate peace.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 422, 93, 'But since, in view of man’s inveterate stupidity, it may not be settled for another thousand years, anyone who already knows the truth is permitted to settle things for himself, absolutely as he wishes, on the new principles.', 'Because humanity is too foolish to evolve quickly, Ivan\'s philosophy dictates that enlightened individuals can bypass morality immediately.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 423, 93, 'In this sense, “everything is permitted” to him.', 'This is the core of Ivan\'s dangerous philosophy: without God, the elite are unbound by moral laws.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 424, 93, 'Moreover, since God and immortality do not exist in any case, even if this period should never come, the new man is allowed to become a man-god, though it be he alone in the whole world, and of course, in this new rank, to jump lightheartedly over any former moral obstacle of the former slave-man, if need be.', 'Even if society never changes, the enlightened atheist can act as a god, breaking any rules of the inferior, religious masses.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 425, 93, 'There is no law for God!', 'He asserts that supreme beings are above morality.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 426, 93, 'Where God stands—there is the place of God!', 'He uses circular logic to justify absolute power.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 427, 93, 'Where I stand, there at once will be the foremost place ... “everything is permitted,” and that’s that! ‘', 'He concludes Ivan\'s terrifying rationalization for absolute, immoral freedom.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 428, 93, 'It’s all very nice; only if one wants to swindle, why, I wonder, should one also need the sanction of truth?', 'The devil brilliantly critiques Ivan\'s philosophy: if you just want to act selfishly, why bother dressing it up as a grand, philosophical truth?', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 429, 93, 'But such is the modern little Russian man: without such a sanction, he doesn’t even dare to swindle, so much does he love the truth...”', 'He mocks the hypocrisy of Russian intellectuals, who are too cowardly to commit crimes without first inventing a complex ethical system to justify them.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 430, 94, 'The visitor spoke, obviously carried away by his own eloquence, raising his voice more and more, and glancing sidelong at his host; but he did not manage to finish: Ivan suddenly snatched a glass from the table and flung it at the orator.', 'As the apparition revels in its devastating critique, Ivan snaps under the pressure and violently throws a glass at it.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 431, 95, '“Ah, mais c’est bête enfin!”326 the latter exclaimed, jumping up from the sofa and shaking the spatters of tea off himself.', 'The hallucination reacts with French indignation, physically responding to the thrown tea.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 432, 95, '“He remembered Luther’s inkstand!327', 'The devil compares Ivan\'s action to Martin Luther, who famously threw an inkwell at the devil during a hallucination.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 433, 95, 'He considers me a dream and he throws glasses at a dream!', 'The visitor mocks the illogical nature of physically attacking a hallucination.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 434, 95, 'Just like a woman!', 'He throws in a misogynistic insult regarding Ivan\'s emotional reaction.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 435, 95, 'I knew you were only pretending to stop your ears and were really listening...”', 'He smugly notes that Ivan throwing the glass proves he was still hanging on every word.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 436, 95, 'Suddenly there came a firm, insistent knocking on the window from outside.', 'The psychological tension is abruptly shattered by a real, physical sound from outside the house.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 437, 95, 'Ivan Fyodorovich jumped up from the sofa.', 'Ivan is startled back into reality by the noise.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 438, 96, '“Listen, you’d better open,” the visitor cried, “it’s your brother Alyosha with the most unexpected and interesting news, I guarantee it!”', 'The apparition incorporates the real-world knocking into the hallucination, predicting Alyosha\'s arrival with dire news.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 439, 97, '“Shut up, deceiver, I knew it was Alyosha without you, I had a presentiment of him, and of course he hasn’t come for no reason, of course he has ‘news’!” Ivan exclaimed frenziedly.', 'Ivan desperately tries to reclaim his rationality, insisting he deduced it was Alyosha himself and doesn\'t need the devil\'s prophecies.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 440, 98, '“But open, open to him.', 'The visitor urges Ivan to answer the window.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 441, 98, 'There’s a blizzard out there, and he’s your brother.', 'He points out the harsh weather and familial duty.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 442, 98, 'Monsieur sait-il le temps qu’il fait?', 'He asks in French if Ivan knows the weather outside.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 443, 98, 'C’est à ne pas mettre un chien dehors ... “328', 'He completes the French idiom, stating it\'s weather not fit for a dog.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 444, 99, 'The knocking continued.', 'The urgent sound from the real world persists.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 445, 99, 'Ivan wanted to rush to the window; but something seemed suddenly to bind his legs and arms.', 'Ivan experiences sleep paralysis or a severe physical manifestation of his breakdown, unable to move.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 446, 99, 'He was straining as hard as he could to break his bonds, but in vain.', 'He fights desperately against his own unresponsive body.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 447, 99, 'The knocking on the window grew stronger and louder.', 'Alyosha\'s urgency outside increases.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 448, 99, 'At last the bonds broke and Ivan Fyodorovich jumped up from the sofa.', 'Ivan\'s physical paralysis suddenly snaps, allowing him to move.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 449, 99, 'He looked around wildly.', 'He urgently surveys the room to ground himself in reality.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 450, 99, 'The two candles were almost burnt down, the glass he had just thrown at his visitor stood before him on the table, and there was no one on the opposite sofa.', 'The physical evidence proves the hallucination was entirely internal: the glass was never thrown, time has passed, and the room is empty.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 451, 99, 'The knocking on the window continued insistently, but not at all as loudly as he had just imagined in his dream, on the contrary, it was quite restrained.', 'He realizes his mind had amplified the sound of Alyosha\'s knocking to fit the dramatic intensity of his nightmare.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 452, 100, '“That was no dream!', 'Ivan, still reeling from the vividness of the vision, struggles to accept it wasn\'t real.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 453, 100, 'No, I swear it was no dream, it all just happened!” Ivan Fyodorovich cried, rushed to the window, and opened it.', 'In a state of extreme panic and lingering delirium, he throws open the window.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 454, 101, '“Alyosha, I told you not to come!” he cried fiercely to his brother.', 'Ivan lashes out at Alyosha, still aggressive and defensive from his mental battle.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 455, 101, '“Make it short: what do you want?', 'He demands Alyosha deliver his news quickly.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 456, 101, 'Make it short, do you hear?”', 'He impatiently reiterates his demand, unable to handle any more stress.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 457, 102, '“Smerdyakov hanged himself an hour ago,” Alyosha answered from outside.', 'Alyosha delivers the devastating, plot-altering news of the servant\'s suicide.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('11-09', 458, 103, '“Come to the porch, I’ll open at once,” Ivan said, and he went to open the door for Alyosha.', 'Shocked back into grim reality, Ivan instructs his brother to come to the door, abandoning his hallucination to deal with the real-world tragedy.', '2026-07-18 15:50:10', '2026-07-18 15:50:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 1, 1, 'As the superflu epidemic wound down, there was a second epidemic that lasted roughly two weeks.', 'This sentence introduces a new phase following the devastating superflu outbreak. Although the disease itself was ending, another widespread phenomenon emerged. The word *epidemic* is used metaphorically here, suggesting that many people were affected by a common pattern of death even after surviving the flu. The two-week duration emphasizes that this was a distinct but brief period following the main catastrophe.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 2, 1, 'This epidemic was most common in technological societies such as the United States, least common in underdeveloped countries such as Peru or Senegal.', 'The narrator explains that this second wave of deaths occurred more frequently in highly industrialized nations. Technological societies tend to depend heavily on complex systems—electricity, transportation, healthcare, food distribution, and communications. When these systems collapsed after the superflu, survivors became vulnerable. Less developed countries, whose populations often relied less on such infrastructure, experienced fewer deaths from this secondary crisis.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 3, 1, 'In the United States the second epidemic took about 16 percent of the superflu survivors.', 'This sentence quantifies the impact. Even after surviving the deadly superflu, about one-sixth of the remaining population in the United States died during this second phase. The statistic highlights how dangerous the aftermath of societal collapse was.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 4, 1, 'In places like Peru and Senegal, no more than 3 percent.', 'The contrast reinforces the previous point. In poorer countries, far fewer survivors died during the second epidemic. The difference suggests that dependence on modern systems can become a liability when those systems suddenly disappear.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 5, 1, 'The second epidemic had no name because the symptoms differed wildly from case to case.', 'Unlike the superflu, which had recognizable symptoms and a clear cause, this second wave of deaths had many different forms. People died from accidents, starvation, untreated injuries, psychological breakdowns, and other causes. Since there was no single pattern, it never received a specific medical name.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 6, 1, 'A sociologist like Glen Bateman might have called this second epidemic “natural death” or “those ole emergency room blues.”', 'The narrator imagines how Glen Bateman, a sociologist and one of the novel\'s major characters, might interpret these deaths. \"Natural death\" suggests deaths resulting from ordinary vulnerabilities rather than disease. \"Those ole emergency room blues\" humorously refers to situations where people would normally be saved by hospitals or emergency services, but those institutions no longer exist.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 7, 1, 'In a strictly Darwinian sense, it was the final cut—the unkindest cut of all, some might have said.', 'The phrase \"Darwinian\" refers to natural selection, where survival depends on adaptability. Those who survived the superflu still faced another test. The expression \"final cut\" suggests a last process of elimination, removing even more survivors. \"The unkindest cut of all\" emphasizes the cruelty of dying after already surviving the world\'s greatest disaster.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 8, 2, 'Sam Tauber was five and a half years old.', 'This simple sentence establishes Sam as a very young child. His age immediately evokes vulnerability because children depend heavily on adults for survival, guidance, and protection.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 9, 2, 'His mother had died on June the twenty-fourth in the Murfreesboro, Georgia, General Hospital.', 'The first loss in Sam\'s family is presented plainly and factually. The mention of a hospital reminds readers that even medical institutions were powerless against the superflu.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 10, 2, 'On the twenty-fifth, his father and younger sister, two-year-old April, had died.', 'Only one day later, Sam loses both his father and his little sister. The rapid succession of deaths emphasizes the devastating speed of the epidemic and leaves Sam increasingly isolated.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 11, 2, 'On June the twenty-seventh, his older brother Mike died, leaving Sam to shift for himself.', 'Mike\'s death removes Sam\'s last close family member. The phrase \"shift for himself\" means Sam must now survive alone despite being only five years old.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 12, 3, 'Sam had been in shock ever since the death of his mother.', 'Psychological shock has overwhelmed Sam. He cannot fully process what has happened, and his emotional state affects his ability to understand or react appropriately to events around him.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 13, 3, 'He wandered carelessly up and down the streets of Murfreesboro, eating when he was hungry, sometimes crying.', 'Without supervision or purpose, Sam drifts through town. His actions are reduced to basic instincts: eating and expressing grief. The word \"carelessly\" suggests he has little awareness of danger.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 14, 3, 'After a while he stopped crying, because crying did no good.', 'Sam reaches a tragic realization. Even as a child, he understands that expressing grief cannot change reality. This shows emotional exhaustion rather than healing.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 15, 3, 'It didn’t bring the people back.', 'This short sentence reflects a child\'s simple but painful logic. Sam understands that his loved ones are permanently gone.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 16, 3, 'At night his sleep was broken by horrible nightmares in which Papa and April and Mike died over and over, their faces swollen black, a terrible rattling sound in their chests as they strangled on their own snot.', 'Sam is traumatized by vivid memories of the disease. The nightmares force him to relive the deaths repeatedly. The graphic imagery emphasizes both the horror of the superflu and the lasting psychological damage it inflicted.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 17, 4, 'At quarter of ten on the morning of July 2, Sam wandered into a field of wild blackberries behind Hattie Reynolds’s house.', 'The narrative shifts to the final day of Sam\'s life. The precise time creates a sense of inevitability and realism.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 18, 4, 'Bemused and vacant-eyed, he zigzagged among blackberry bushes that were almost twice as tall as he was, picking the berries and eating them until his lips and chin were smeared black.', 'Sam appears confused and emotionally detached. The blackberry bushes tower over him, emphasizing his small size. Eating berries becomes a childlike attempt to satisfy hunger and perhaps find comfort.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 19, 4, 'The thorns ripped at his clothes and sometimes at his bare flesh, but he barely noticed.', 'His physical and emotional numbness is so great that even pain receives little attention. His focus is reduced to basic survival.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 20, 4, 'Bees hummed drowsily around him.', 'This calm natural image contrasts sharply with the tragedy unfolding. Nature continues peacefully despite human suffering.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 21, 4, 'He never saw the old and rotted well-cover half buried in tall grass and blackberry creepers.', 'The danger is introduced. The well-cover is hidden and decayed, making it a deadly trap. Sam\'s distracted condition contributes to his failure to notice it.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 22, 4, 'It gave under his weight with a grinding, splintering crash, and Sam plunged twenty feet down the rock-lined shaft to the dry bottom, where he broke both legs.', 'The accident occurs suddenly. The detailed sounds create vivid imagery. Breaking both legs leaves Sam helpless at the bottom of the abandoned well.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 23, 4, 'He died twenty hours later, as much from fear and misery as from shock and hunger and dehydration.', 'His death is caused not only by physical injuries but also by emotional suffering and isolation. Had society still existed, rescue would likely have been easy. Instead, he dies alone.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 24, 5, 'Irma Fayette lived in Lodi, California.', 'The narrative moves to another victim of the second epidemic. The simple introduction establishes setting and character.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 25, 5, 'She was a lady of twenty-six, a virgin, morbidly afraid of rape.', 'Irma is described through traits that shape her worldview. Her fear of rape is not merely ordinary caution but an obsessive, unhealthy fear that dominates her thinking.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 26, 5, 'Her life had been one long nightmare since June twenty-third, when looting had broken out in town and there had been no police to stop the looters.', 'The collapse of law and order has intensified Irma\'s fears. Without police protection, she feels exposed and endangered.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 27, 5, 'Irma had a small house on a side-street; her mother had lived there with her until she had died of a stroke in 1985.', 'This provides background. Irma already experienced loss before the superflu and lived a relatively isolated life with her mother.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 28, 5, 'When the looting began, and the gunshots, and the horrifying sound of drunken men roaring up and down the streets of the main business section on motorcycles, Irma had locked all the doors and then had hidden in the spare room downstairs.', 'The piling up of frightening details mirrors Irma\'s terror. Her response is retreat and concealment rather than confrontation.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 29, 5, 'Since then she had crept upstairs periodically, quiet as a mouse, to get food or to relieve herself.', 'She has essentially been living in hiding. The simile \"quiet as a mouse\" highlights her fear and secrecy.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 30, 6, 'Irma didn’t like people.', 'This blunt statement summarizes a central aspect of her personality.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 31, 6, 'If everyone on earth had died but her, she would have been perfectly happy.', 'The exaggeration reveals her extreme dislike of human company and social interaction.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 32, 6, 'But that wasn’t the case.', 'Reality disappoints her fantasy. Other people still exist.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 33, 6, 'Only yesterday, after she had begun cautiously to hope that no one was left in Lodi but her, she had seen a gross and drunken man, a hippie man in a T-shirt that said I GAVE UP SEX AND DRINKING AND IT WAS THE SCARIEST 20 MINUTES OF MY LIFE, wandering up the street with a bottle of whiskey in his hand.', 'Her hopes are shattered when she sees another survivor. The detailed description reflects how threatening and repulsive he appears through her eyes.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 34, 6, 'He had long blond hair which cascaded out from under the gimme cap he was wearing and all the way down to his shoulders.', 'The man is depicted as stereotypically countercultural, reinforcing Irma\'s prejudice against him.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 35, 6, 'Tucked into the waistband of his tight bluejeans was a pistol.', 'The weapon increases her fear because it suggests potential violence.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 36, 6, 'Irma had peeked around the bedroom curtain at him until he was out of sight and then had scurried downstairs to the barricaded spare room as if she had been released from a malign spell.', 'She watches him anxiously and then retreats immediately. The comparison to escaping a spell conveys overwhelming relief.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 37, 7, 'They were not all dead.', 'This realization terrifies Irma.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 38, 7, 'If there was one hippie man left, there would be other hippie men.', 'Her thinking becomes generalized and irrational.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 39, 7, 'And they would all be rapers.', 'Her prejudice transforms into certainty. She assumes all such men are predators.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 40, 7, 'They would rape her.', 'Her fear becomes a fixed expectation.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 41, 7, 'Sooner or later they would find her and rape her.', 'She convinces herself that assault is inevitable, illustrating her paranoia.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 42, 8, 'This morning, before first light, she had crept up to the attic, where her father’s few possessions were stored in cardboard boxes.', 'Seeking security, Irma explores belongings connected to her father.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 43, 8, 'Her father had been a merchant seaman.', 'A brief piece of family history.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 44, 8, 'He had deserted Irma’s mother in the late sixties.', 'Irma\'s father abandoned the family, shaping negative family memories.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 45, 8, 'Irma’s mother had told Irma all about it.', 'Irma\'s understanding comes largely from her mother\'s perspective.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 46, 8, 'She had been perfectly frank.', 'Her mother spoke openly and harshly.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 47, 8, 'Her father had been a beast who got drunk and then wanted to rape her.', 'This reflects the mother\'s characterization, which deeply influenced Irma\'s attitudes toward men.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 48, 8, 'They all did.', 'Irma\'s mother generalized from one man to all men.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 49, 8, 'When you got married, that gave a man the right to rape you anytime he wanted.', 'This reflects a deeply distorted and cynical belief about marriage and male behavior.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 50, 8, 'Even in the daytime.', 'The absurd emphasis reveals bitterness and resentment.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 51, 8, 'Irma’s mother always summed up her husband’s desertion in three words, the same words Irma could have applied to the death of almost every man, woman, and child on the face of the earth: “No great loss.”', 'The phrase shows emotional coldness. Irma has inherited much of her mother\'s contempt for humanity.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 52, 9, 'Most of the boxes contained nothing but cheap trinkets bought in foreign ports—Souvenir of Hong Kong, Souvenir of Saigon, Souvenir of Copenhagen.', 'Irma discovers that most of her father\'s belongings are insignificant souvenirs collected during his travels. The list of cities emphasizes his wandering life as a sailor. To Irma, these objects have little emotional value and serve mainly as reminders of a man she never respected.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 53, 9, 'There was a scrapbook of photographs.', 'Among the possessions is something more personal: a collection of photographs that preserve moments from her father\'s life.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 54, 9, 'Most of them showed her father on ship, sometimes smiling into the camera with his arms about the shoulders of his fellow beasts.', 'The photographs depict her father and his companions enjoying themselves aboard ship. However, the phrase \"fellow beasts\" reflects Irma\'s contemptuous view of men, a perspective inherited from her mother. Even innocent photographs are filtered through her prejudice.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 55, 9, 'Well, probably the disease that they were calling Captain Trips out here had struck him down in whatever place he had run off to.', 'Irma assumes that her father has died from the superflu, commonly called \"Captain Trips.\" She imagines him dying somewhere far away, where he disappeared years before.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 56, 9, 'No great loss.', 'This phrase echoes her mother\'s favorite judgment. It demonstrates Irma\'s emotional detachment and lack of sympathy for her father.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 57, 10, 'But there was one wooden box with small gold hinges on it, and in this box was a gun.', 'Among the otherwise unimportant possessions, Irma finds something that immediately captures her attention: a firearm. This discovery marks a turning point in her story.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 58, 10, 'A .45 caliber pistol.', 'The narrator identifies the weapon specifically, emphasizing that it is a powerful handgun.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 59, 10, 'It lay on red velvet, and in a secret compartment below the red velvet were some bullets.', 'The gun is presented almost like a treasured heirloom. The hidden compartment suggests careful storage and perhaps a sense of mystery surrounding the weapon.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 60, 10, 'They were green and mossy-looking, but Irma thought they would work all right.', 'The bullets show signs of age and corrosion. Nevertheless, Irma assumes they remain functional, despite having no real expertise.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 61, 10, 'Bullets were metal.', 'This is Irma\'s simple reasoning process.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 62, 10, 'They didn’t spoil like milk or cheese.', 'She compares ammunition to food. Her logic seems sensible to her, but the comparison reveals her lack of understanding about firearms and ammunition.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 63, 11, 'She loaded the gun under the single cobwebby attic bulb, and then went down to eat her breakfast at her own kitchen table.', 'After arming herself, Irma behaves with new confidence. The image of the dusty attic bulb contributes to the atmosphere of neglect and decay.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 64, 11, 'She would not hide like a mouse in a hole any longer.', 'The gun gives her a sense of empowerment. She decides to stop living in fear and hiding.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 65, 11, 'She was armed.', 'This short sentence reflects her belief that possessing a weapon has fundamentally changed her situation.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 66, 11, 'Let the rapers beware.', 'Irma now sees herself as the dangerous one. Her fear has transformed into defiant confidence, though it rests on shaky assumptions.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 67, 12, 'That afternoon she went out on the front porch to read her book.', 'This is a dramatic change in behavior. Instead of hiding indoors, she openly occupies a visible space outside her house.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 68, 12, 'The name of the book was Satan Is Alive and Well on the Planet Earth.', 'The title reflects themes of moral corruption and judgment, which align with Irma\'s worldview.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 69, 12, 'It was grim and joyful stuff.', 'The book combines frightening descriptions of evil with satisfaction at the punishment of sinners.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 70, 12, 'The sinners and the ingrates had gotten their just deserts, just as the book said they would.', 'Irma interprets the global catastrophe as divine punishment. She believes people received what they deserved.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 71, 12, 'They were all gone.', 'From her perspective, humanity has largely been wiped out.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 72, 12, 'Except for a few hippie rapers, and she guessed she could handle them.', 'Although she still fears certain survivors, she now believes she has the means to defend herself.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 73, 12, 'The gun was by her side.', 'The pistol serves as both protection and a symbol of her newfound confidence.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 74, 13, 'At two o’clock the man with the blond hair came back.', 'The survivor Irma saw earlier reappears, creating the confrontation she has dreaded.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 75, 13, 'He was so drunk he could hardly stand up.', 'The man is heavily intoxicated and physically unsteady.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 76, 13, 'He saw Irma and his face lighted, no doubt thinking of how lucky he had been to finally discover some “pussy.”', 'The narration briefly enters Irma\'s interpretation of his reaction. She assumes his interest is sexual and predatory, although the truth remains uncertain.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 77, 13, '“Hey, baby!” he cried. “It’s just you and me! How long—”', 'The man appears excited to find another survivor. His sentence is interrupted before he can finish.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 78, 13, 'Then terror clouded his face as he saw Irma put down her book and raise the .45.', 'His mood instantly changes from excitement to fear when he realizes she is pointing a gun at him.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 79, 14, '“Hey, listen, put that thing down... is it loaded? Hey—!”', 'The man desperately tries to calm the situation. His questions reveal sudden panic and concern about the weapon.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 80, 15, 'Irma pulled the trigger.', 'Believing she is defending herself, Irma fires the pistol.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 81, 15, 'The pistol exploded, killing her instantly.', 'The old, poorly maintained weapon catastrophically fails. Instead of shooting the man, it explodes and kills Irma herself. The irony is tragic: the object she trusted for protection becomes the cause of her death.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 82, 15, 'No great loss.', 'The narrator repeats Irma\'s own phrase. The repetition is darkly ironic, applying her harsh judgment to her own death.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 83, 16, 'George McDougall lived in Nyack, New York.', 'The narrative shifts to another survivor whose death belongs to the \"second epidemic.\"', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 84, 16, 'He had been a teacher of high school mathematics, specializing in remedial work.', 'George is introduced as an educator who helped struggling students. This detail portrays him as patient and caring.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 85, 16, 'He and his wife had been practicing Catholics, and Harriett McDougall had borne him eleven children, nine boys and two girls.', 'George\'s large family and religious faith are central aspects of his identity.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 86, 16, 'So between June 22, when his nine-year-old son Jeff had succumbed to what was then diagnosed as “flu-related pneumonia,” and June 29, when his sixteen-year-old daughter Patricia (and oh God she had been so young and so achingly beautiful) had succumbed to what everyone—those that were left—was then calling tube-neck, he had seen the twelve people he loved best in the world pass away while he himself remained healthy and feeling fine.', 'This devastating sentence summarizes George\'s tragedy. Over one week he loses his wife and all eleven children while remaining healthy himself. The parenthetical comment about Patricia reveals the depth of his grief.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 87, 16, 'He had joked at school about not being able to remember all his kids’ names, but the order of their passing was engraved on his memory: Jeff on the twenty-second, Marty and Helen on the twenty-third, his wife Harriett and Bill and George, Jr., and Robert and Stan on the twenty-fourth, Richard on the twenty-fifth, Danny on the twenty-seventh, three-year-old Frank on the twenty-eighth, and finally Pat—and Pat had seemed to be getting better, right up to the end.', 'The painful list demonstrates how vividly George remembers each death. The irony is cruel: although he once joked about keeping track of so many children, he now remembers every loss with perfect clarity.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 88, 17, 'George thought he would go mad.', 'The accumulated grief feels unbearable. He fears losing his sanity under the weight of loss.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 89, 18, 'He had begun jogging ten years before, on his doctor’s advice.', 'The narrative introduces jogging as a long-standing habit.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 90, 18, 'He didn’t play tennis or handball, paid a kid (one of his, of course) to mow the lawn, and usually drove to the corner store when Harriett needed a loaf of bread.', 'George once lived a relatively sedentary lifestyle. The parenthetical remark gently reminds readers of the large family he used to have.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 91, 18, 'You’re putting on weight, Dr. Warner had said.', 'The doctor\'s warning initiated the change.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 92, 18, 'Lead in the seat.', 'This colloquial expression means spending too much time sitting.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 93, 18, 'No good for your heart.', 'The doctor warns of health consequences.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 94, 18, 'Try jogging.', 'The solution is simple and practical.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 95, 19, 'So he had gotten a sweatsuit and had gone jogging every night, for short distances at the start, then longer and longer ones.', 'George gradually developed the habit and improved his endurance.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 96, 19, 'At first he’d felt self-conscious, sure that the neighbors must be tapping their foreheads and rolling their eyes, and then a couple of the men that he had only known to wave to when they were out watering their lawns came and asked if they could join him—probably there was safety in numbers.', 'His initial embarrassment faded as others joined him, turning a personal activity into a community one.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 97, 19, 'By that time, George’s two oldest boys had also joined in.', 'His sons participated as well, making jogging a family activity.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 98, 19, 'It became a sort of neighborhood thing, and although the membership was always evolving as people dropped in and dropped out, it stayed a neighborhood thing.', 'Jogging created social bonds and community spirit. The memory becomes especially poignant because that community no longer exists.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 99, 20, 'Now that everyone was gone, he still jogged.', 'His habit survives even after society and his family have vanished.', '2026-07-19 15:51:09', '2026-07-19 15:51:09');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 100, 20, 'Every day.', 'The short sentence emphasizes consistency and desperation.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 101, 20, 'For hours.', 'His jogging has become excessive and obsessive.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 102, 20, 'It was only when he was jogging, concentrating on nothing more than the thud of his tennis shoes on the sidewalk and the swing of his arms and his steady harsh respiration, that he lost that feeling of impending madness.', 'Running serves as psychological escape. Physical exertion temporarily silences his grief.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 103, 20, 'He could not commit suicide because as a practicing Catholic he knew that suicide was a mortal sin and God must be saving him for something, so he jogged.', 'His religious beliefs prevent self-destruction. Running becomes his substitute for despair.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 104, 20, 'Yesterday he had jogged for almost six hours, until he was completely out of breath and almost retching with exhaustion.', 'His coping mechanism is becoming physically dangerous.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 105, 20, 'He was fifty-one, not a young man anymore, and he supposed that so much running was not good for him, but in another, more important way, it was the only thing that was any good.', 'He recognizes the physical risks but values jogging because it is the only thing preserving his mental stability. I can continue with the remaining paragraphs (beginning **“So he had gotten up this morning at first light...”** through **Arthur Stimson’s death**) in the next response.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 106, 21, 'So he had gotten up this morning at first light after a mostly sleepless night (the thought that played over and over in his mind was: Jeff-Marty-Helen-Harriett-Bill-George-Junior-Robert-Stanley-Richard-Danny-Frank-Patty-and-I-thought-she-was-getting-better) and put on his sweatsuit.', 'George begins another day burdened by grief. He has slept very little because his mind continually replays the names of his dead family members. The uninterrupted list mirrors the relentless cycle of thoughts tormenting him. The final phrase, *\"and-I-thought-she-was-getting-better,\"* reveals how Patricia\'s death remains especially painful because he had briefly believed she would survive.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 107, 21, 'He went out and began to jog up and down the deserted streets of Nyack, his feet sometimes gritting on broken glass, once leaping over a TV set that lay shattered on the pavement, taking him past residential streets where the shades were drawn and also past the horrible three-car crash at the Main Street intersection.', 'The abandoned town reflects the collapse of civilization. Broken glass, wrecked property, and an unrecovered traffic accident all testify to the sudden disappearance of social order. George runs through a landscape that has become a graveyard of ordinary life. The closed shades suggest homes filled with death or emptiness.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 108, 22, 'He jogged at first, but it became necessary to run faster and faster to keep the thoughts behind him.', 'George\'s running is no longer exercise; it is an attempt to outrun his grief. As painful memories pursue him mentally, he feels compelled to increase his speed.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 109, 22, 'He jogged and then he trotted and then he ran and finally he sprinted, a fifty-one-year-old man with gray hair in a gray sweatsuit and white tennis shoes, fleeing up and down empty streets as if all the devils of hell were after him.', 'The gradual progression from jogging to sprinting illustrates escalating desperation. The image of an older man racing through deserted streets is tragic and symbolic. The comparison to being chased by devils shows that the true pursuit comes from his own anguish, guilt, and memories.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 110, 22, 'At quarter past eleven he suffered a massive coronary thrombosis and fell down dead on the corner of Oak and Pine, near a fire plug.', 'George\'s body finally gives out. A coronary thrombosis is a blockage of blood flow to the heart, resulting in a fatal heart attack. His death comes not from disease but from physical and emotional exhaustion.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 111, 22, 'The expression on his face was very like gratitude.', 'This haunting final sentence suggests that death may have brought George relief from unbearable suffering. Rather than fear or pain, his final expression resembles thankfulness, implying release from grief.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 112, 23, 'Mrs. Eileen Drummond of Clewiston, Florida, got very drunk on DeKuyper crème de menthe on the afternoon of July 2.', 'The narrative shifts to another survivor. Eileen responds to tragedy through alcohol. The specific mention of crème de menthe gives the scene a realistic, ordinary quality despite the extraordinary circumstances.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 113, 23, 'She wanted to get drunk because if she was drunk she wouldn’t have to think about her family, and crème de menthe was the only kind of alcohol she could stand.', 'Her drinking is motivated by a desire to escape emotional pain. She is trying to numb herself rather than enjoy alcohol. The detail about her preference for crème de menthe emphasizes her ordinary habits and personality.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 114, 23, 'She had found a baggie filled with marijuana in her sixteen-year-old’s room the day before and had succeeded in getting stoned, but being stoned only seemed to make things worse.', 'Previously, she had tried another form of escape through marijuana. Instead of helping, it intensified her emotional suffering.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 115, 23, 'She had sat in her living room all afternoon, stoned and crying over photographs in her scrapbook.', 'The photographs force her to confront memories of her family. Rather than forgetting, she becomes overwhelmed by grief and spends hours crying.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 116, 24, 'So this afternoon she drank a whole bottle of crème de menthe and then got sick and threw up in the bathroom and then went to bed and lit a cigarette and fell asleep and burned the house down and she didn’t have to think about it anymore, ever.', 'The sentence rushes forward without pauses, mirroring the unstoppable chain of events. Eileen drinks excessively, becomes ill, falls asleep while smoking, and accidentally starts a fatal fire. The final phrase, *\"she didn’t have to think about it anymore, ever,\"* is darkly ironic because death permanently ends her suffering.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 117, 24, 'The wind had freshened, and she also burned down most of Clewiston.', 'The tragedy extends beyond her own death. Strong winds spread the flames, causing massive destruction throughout the town.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 118, 24, 'No great loss.', 'The narrator repeats the phrase used earlier with bitter irony. In the context of a nearly empty world, the destruction of a town seems insignificant compared to humanity\'s overall collapse.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 119, 25, 'Arthur Stimson lived in Reno, Nevada.', 'Another brief introduction presents a final example of the second epidemic.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 120, 25, 'On the afternoon of the twenty-ninth, after swimming in Lake Tahoe, he stepped on a rusty nail.', 'The event that leads to Arthur\'s death begins with a common accident. Under normal circumstances, such an injury would likely be minor and easily treated.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 121, 25, 'The wound turned gangrenous.', 'Without proper medical care, the infection becomes severe. Gangrene involves the death and decay of body tissue and can quickly become life-threatening.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 122, 25, 'He diagnosed the trouble by smell and tried to amputate his foot.', 'Arthur realizes the seriousness of the infection and attempts drastic self-treatment. The fact that he identifies gangrene by its odor highlights both the severity of the condition and the absence of doctors.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 123, 25, 'Halfway through the operation he fainted and died of shock and blood loss in the lobby of Toby Harrah’s gambling casino, where he had attempted the operation.', 'Arthur\'s desperate attempt to save himself ends in disaster. Without anesthesia, surgical equipment, or medical assistance, he loses consciousness and dies from physical trauma and bleeding. The location—a casino lobby—underscores the collapse of normal society, where people are forced to perform surgery on themselves in public spaces because no hospitals or medical professionals remain.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 124, 26, 'In Swanville, Maine, a ten-year-old girl named Candice Moran fell off her bike and died of a fractured skull.', 'This brief sentence presents another example of the \"second epidemic.\" Candice survives the superflu but dies from an ordinary childhood accident. Under normal circumstances, emergency medical services might have saved her. The tragedy illustrates how the collapse of society turns minor or survivable accidents into fatal events. Her age also emphasizes the vulnerability of children in a world without adults and institutions to protect them.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 125, 27, 'Milton Craslow, a rancher in Harding County, New Mexico, was bitten by a rattlesnake and died half an hour later.', 'Like Candice\'s death, Milton\'s death results from a common danger rather than disease. In normal times, medical treatment such as antivenom might have saved him. The sentence reinforces the theme that many survivors of the superflu ultimately died because the systems that normally support human life no longer existed.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 126, 28, 'In Milltown, Kentucky, Judy Horton was quite pleased with events.', 'This opening sentence immediately sets Judy apart from the previous victims. While most survivors are devastated by loss, Judy feels satisfied with recent events. The statement creates curiosity about why she would react positively to a global catastrophe.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 127, 28, 'Judy was seventeen years old and pretty.', 'The narrator provides basic information about Judy. Her youth is important because many of her decisions and attitudes reflect immaturity and self-centeredness.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 128, 28, 'Two years before, she had made two serious mistakes: she had allowed herself to get pregnant, and she had allowed her parents to talk her into marrying the boy responsible, a four-eyes engineering student from the state university.', 'Judy views both her pregnancy and her marriage as mistakes. The phrase \"four-eyes\" is a childish insult aimed at her husband, revealing her resentment and lack of maturity. She sees herself as trapped by decisions made when she was younger.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 129, 28, 'At fifteen she had been flattered just to be asked out by a college man (even if he was only a freshman) and for the life of her she couldn’t remember why she had allowed Waldo—Waldo Horton, what a yuck name—to “work his will” on her.', 'Judy recalls being impressed simply because an older college student showed interest in her. Looking back, she cannot understand why she became involved with Waldo. Her repeated contempt for his name demonstrates how deeply she dislikes him.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 130, 28, 'And if she was going to be knocked up, why did it have to be him?', 'This rhetorical question expresses her frustration about becoming pregnant. She regrets not only the pregnancy itself but also the identity of the father.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 131, 28, 'Judy had also allowed Steve Phillips and Mark Collins to “work their will” on her; they were both on the Milltown High football team (the Milltown Cougars, to be exact, fight-fight-fight-fight-for-the-dear-blue-and-white) and she was a cheerleader.', 'The sentence reveals that Judy had relationships with other boys as well. The cheerleader and football-player details evoke a stereotypical high-school social world. The school chant reflects her nostalgic attachment to that lifestyle.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 132, 28, 'If it hadn’t been for yucky old Waldo Horton, she would have made head cheerleader her junior year, easy.', 'Judy blames Waldo and the pregnancy for disrupting the future she imagined for herself. She focuses on lost social status rather than deeper consequences.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 133, 28, 'And, getting back to the point, either Steve or Mark would have made more acceptable husbands.', 'In Judy\'s mind, appearance and popularity matter more than responsibility or character. She evaluates potential husbands in superficial terms.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 134, 28, 'They both had broad shoulders and Mark had stone bitchin shoulder-length blond hair.', 'Her description reflects teenage priorities. Physical attractiveness dominates her thinking.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 135, 28, 'But it was Waldo, it could have been no one but Waldo.', 'Despite her wishes, she knows Waldo is unquestionably the father.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 136, 28, 'All she had to do was look in her diary and do the arithmetic.', 'The diary provides evidence of when her relationships occurred, making the father\'s identity obvious.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 137, 28, 'And after the baby came she wouldn’t have even had to do that.', 'Once the child was born, any uncertainty disappeared.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 138, 28, 'It looked just like him.', 'The baby\'s resemblance to Waldo confirms the truth.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 139, 28, 'Yucky.', 'This single-word sentence summarizes Judy\'s disgust. It is childish and cruel, reinforcing her immature personality.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 140, 29, 'So for two long years she had struggled along, through a variety of crummy jobs in fast-food restaurants and motels, while Waldo went to school.', 'Judy feels burdened by responsibility. While she works low-paying jobs, Waldo continues his education, creating resentment.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 141, 29, 'It got so she hated Waldo’s school most of all, even more than the baby and Waldo himself.', 'Her bitterness becomes irrational. She transfers her frustration onto the university because it symbolizes the future Waldo is working toward while she feels trapped.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 142, 29, 'If he wanted a family so bad, why couldn’t he get out and work?', 'She believes Waldo should have abandoned school and become the family\'s primary provider.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 143, 29, 'She had.', 'This short sentence emphasizes her sense of injustice. She sees herself as carrying the burden alone.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 144, 29, 'But her parents and his wouldn’t allow it.', 'The older generation supported Waldo\'s education, believing it would benefit the family later.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 145, 29, 'Alone, Judy could have sweet-talked him into it (she would have gotten him to promise before she let him touch her in bed), but all four of the in-laws had their noses in things all the time.', 'She believes she could have manipulated Waldo if family members had not interfered. The statement reveals both her frustration and her tendency toward manipulation.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 146, 29, 'Oh Judy, things will be so much better when Waldo has a good job.', 'This sentence mimics advice she repeatedly heard from others.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 147, 29, 'Oh Judy, things would look so much brighter if you’d go to church more often.', 'Another example of unwanted advice, which she dismisses.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 148, 29, 'Oh Judy, eat shit and keep smiling until you get it down.', 'This vulgar expression shows how she interprets all such advice—as demands that she endure unhappiness quietly.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 149, 29, 'Until you get it all down.', 'The repetition intensifies her bitterness and anger.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 150, 30, 'Then the superflu had come along and had solved all her problems.', 'From Judy\'s perspective, the epidemic has removed the obstacles she hated. This statement is deeply ironic because it treats mass death as a solution.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 151, 30, 'Her parents had died, her little boy Petie had died (that was sort of sad, but she got over it in a couple of days), then Waldo’s parents had died, and finally Waldo himself had died and she was free.', 'The sentence exposes Judy\'s shocking emotional detachment. She grieves briefly for her son but quickly moves on. The deaths of everyone else are presented as liberating.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 152, 30, 'The thought that she herself might die had never crossed her mind, and of course she didn’t.', 'Judy never seriously considers her own mortality. Ironically, she survives the disease itself.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 153, 31, 'They had been living in a large and rambling apartment house in downtown Milltown.', 'The narrator shifts to the circumstances that will lead to Judy\'s death.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 154, 31, 'One of the features of the place that sold Waldo on it (Judy, of course, didn’t have a say) was a large walk-in meat freezer in the basement.', 'The freezer becomes an important detail. Judy\'s complaint that she had no say reflects ongoing resentment toward Waldo.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 155, 31, 'They had taken the apartment in September of 1988, and their apartment was on the third floor, and who always seemed to get stuck taking the roast and the hamburger down to the freezer?', 'The rhetorical question prepares for another complaint.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 156, 31, 'Three guesses and the first two don’t count.', 'The answer is obviously Judy. The sarcastic expression emphasizes her annoyance.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 157, 31, 'Waldo and Petie had died at home.', 'This sentence returns to the aftermath of the epidemic.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 158, 31, 'By that time you couldn’t get hospital service unless you were a bigwig and the mortuaries were swamped (creepy old places anyway, Judy wouldn’t go near one on a bet), but the power was still on.', 'Medical and funeral services had collapsed, leaving Judy with few options for dealing with the bodies.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 159, 31, 'So she had taken them downstairs and put them in the freezer.', 'The freezer becomes a makeshift morgue.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 160, 32, 'The power had gone off in Milltown three days ago, but it was still fairly cool down there.', 'Although refrigeration no longer works, the basement remains somewhat cool.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 161, 32, 'Judy knew because she went down to look at their dead bodies three or four times a day.', 'This surprising habit suggests a complicated psychological attachment to the dead.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 162, 32, 'She told herself she was just checking.', 'She attempts to rationalize her behavior.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 163, 32, 'What else could it be?', 'She questions her own motives.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 164, 32, 'Surely she wasn’t gloating?', 'The question hints that she may secretly take satisfaction in her freedom from her husband and child.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 165, 33, 'She went down on the afternoon of July 2 and forgot to put the rubber wedge under the freezer door.', 'A small mistake triggers disaster. The ordinary nature of the error makes it especially tragic.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 166, 33, 'The door swung shut behind her and latched.', 'The danger becomes immediate. She is trapped.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 167, 33, 'It was then that she noticed, after two years of coming and going down here, that there was no inside knob on the freezer door.', 'The cruel irony is that she discovers this fatal flaw only after it is too late.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 168, 33, 'By then it was too warm to freeze, but not too cold to starve.', 'The freezer no longer functions as a freezer, but it remains an inescapable prison. She will die slowly rather than quickly.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 169, 33, 'So Judy Horton died in the company of her son and husband after all.', 'The ending is darkly ironic. After viewing their deaths as liberation, she ultimately dies beside them. The freedom she celebrated becomes meaningless.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 170, 34, 'Jim Lee of Hattiesburg, Mississippi, hooked up all the electrical outlets in his house to a gasoline generator and then electrocuted himself trying to start it up.', 'Jim\'s death results from a technical mistake. Like many second-epidemic deaths, it would likely have been preventable if help or expertise had been available. The sentence illustrates how dangerous ordinary tasks become when society collapses.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 171, 35, 'Richard Hoggins was a young black man who had lived his entire life in Detroit, Michigan.', 'The narrative introduces another survivor, establishing his background.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 172, 35, 'He had been addicted to the fine white powder he called “hehrawn” for the last five years.', 'The altered pronunciation reflects street slang for heroin. Addiction has dominated his life.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 173, 35, 'During the actual superflu epidemic, he had gone through extreme withdrawal as all the pushers and users he knew died or fled.', 'The collapse of the drug trade forced Richard into withdrawal. He suffered not only from society\'s collapse but also from the sudden loss of access to heroin.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 174, 36, 'On this bright summer afternoon he was sitting on a littered stoop, drinking a warm 7-Up and wishing he had a pop, just a small, minor skinpop.', 'Richard sits in a decaying urban environment, craving heroin. Even after enduring withdrawal, he still longs for another injection. I can continue with the remaining Richard Hoggins paragraphs (beginning **“He begin to think about Allie McFarlane...”** through **“He was dead six minutes later.”**) in the next response.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 175, 37, 'He begin to think about Allie McFarlane, and something he had heard about Allie on the streets, just before the shit hit the fan.', 'As Richard sits craving heroin, his thoughts turn to Allie McFarlane, a major drug dealer. The phrase *\"before the shit hit the fan\"* refers to the period immediately before society collapsed due to the superflu. Richard remembers rumors from that time, hoping they might lead him to drugs.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 176, 37, 'People were saying that Allie, who was about the third-biggest in Detroit, had just gotten a fine shipment.', 'The rumor concerned a large and valuable heroin delivery. Allie was an important figure in Detroit\'s drug trade, making the information seem believable and significant.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 177, 37, 'Everybody was going to get well.', 'Among addicts, *\"getting well\"* means taking drugs and ending withdrawal symptoms. The sentence reflects the language and mindset of addiction, where heroin is seen as a cure rather than a problem.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 178, 37, 'None of that brown shit.', 'The rumor claimed the shipment was not low-quality heroin. Richard recalls the distinction with excitement.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 179, 37, 'China White, all kinds of the stuff.', '\"China White\" refers to an especially pure and powerful form of heroin. The mention of it intensifies Richard\'s desire because such drugs are highly valued among users.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 180, 38, 'Richie didn’t know for sure where McFarlane would keep a big order like that—it wasn’t healthy to know about such things—but he had heard it said at different times in passing that if the cops ever got a search-writ for the Grosse Pointe house that Allie had bought for his great-uncle, Allie would go away until the new moon turned to gold.', 'Richard has only vague information about the possible location of the heroin. The phrase *\"it wasn\'t healthy to know about such things\"* means that people involved in criminal enterprises often avoid learning too much because knowledge can become dangerous. The rumor suggests that Allie hid drugs in a house owned by a relative in Grosse Pointe. The colorful expression *\"until the new moon turned to gold\"* means Allie would spend a very long time in prison if the drugs were discovered.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 181, 39, 'Richie decided to take a walk up to Grosse Pointe.', 'His craving turns into action. The possibility that the heroin might still be there is enough motivation for him to make the trip.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 182, 39, 'After all, there was nothing better to do.', 'This statement reflects both the emptiness of the post-apocalyptic world and Richard\'s lack of purpose. With society gone, the search for drugs becomes the most meaningful thing he can imagine.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 183, 40, 'He got the Lake Shore Drive address of one Erin D. McFarlane from the Detroit phone book and walked out there.', 'Richard uses the phone book to locate the property and begins the journey on foot. The detail highlights how much of civilization\'s infrastructure still physically exists even though society itself has collapsed.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 184, 40, 'It was almost dark by the time he made it and his feet hurt.', 'The trip is long and physically exhausting. His determination reveals the power of his addiction.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 185, 40, 'He was no longer trying to tell himself that this was just a casual stroll; he wanted to shoot and he wanted to bad.', 'Richard stops pretending that he is merely curious. He openly acknowledges his desperate desire for heroin. The grammatical roughness reflects his inner voice and urgency.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 186, 41, 'There was a gray fieldstone wall around the estate and Richie went over it like a black shadow, cutting his hands on the broken glass embedded in the top.', 'The estate is protected by a wall topped with broken glass, a common security measure. Richard ignores the danger and injures himself while climbing over it. The description *\"like a black shadow\"* emphasizes stealth and determination.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 187, 41, 'When he broke a window to gain entry, a burglar alarm went off, causing him to flee halfway down the lawn before he remembered there were no cops to answer.', 'The alarm briefly triggers old habits and fears. Even though society has collapsed, Richard instinctively reacts as if the police still exist.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 188, 41, 'He came back, jittery and slicked with sweat.', 'After realizing there is no longer any law enforcement, he returns. Nevertheless, the experience leaves him nervous and physically stressed.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 189, 42, 'The main power was off, and there were easily twenty rooms in the fucking place.', 'The mansion is enormous and dark because electricity is gone. Richard immediately recognizes how difficult it will be to search such a large property.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 190, 42, 'He’d have to wait until tomorrow to look properly, and it would still take three weeks to dump the place upside down in the proper way.', 'He estimates that a thorough search would require an enormous amount of time and effort. The expression *\"dump the place upside down\"* means searching every possible hiding place.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 191, 42, 'And the stuff probably wasn’t even here.', 'Doubt begins to creep in. The heroin may not exist at this location at all.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 192, 42, 'Christ.', 'This brief exclamation expresses frustration and despair.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 193, 42, 'Richie felt sick despair wave through him.', 'The possibility of failure hits him emotionally. His craving makes the thought of not finding heroin almost unbearable.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 194, 42, 'But he would at least look in the obvious places.', 'Despite discouragement, he decides to continue searching. Hope remains stronger than doubt.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 195, 43, 'And in the upstairs bathroom, he found a dozen large plastic bags bulging with white powder.', 'Richard\'s search succeeds almost immediately. The discovery is astonishing because the amount of heroin is enormous.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 196, 43, 'They were in the toilet tank, that old standby.', 'The drugs are hidden in a stereotypical hiding place. The phrase *\"that old standby\"* suggests this is a familiar trick among criminals.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 197, 43, 'Richie stared at them, sick with desire, dimly thinking that Allie must have been greasing all the right people if he could afford to leave a stash like this in a fucking toilet tank.', 'Richard is overwhelmed by craving. At the same time, he marvels at the scale of the operation. *\"Greasing all the right people\"* means bribing officials or influential individuals to avoid trouble.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 198, 43, 'There was enough dope here to last one man sixteen centuries.', 'This is an exaggeration emphasizing the enormous quantity of heroin. Richard has discovered far more than he could ever personally use.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 199, 44, 'He took one bag into the master bedroom and broke it open on the bedspread.', 'Unable to resist, Richard immediately prepares to use the drug.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 200, 44, 'His hands trembled as he got his works out and cooked up.', 'His shaking hands reveal excitement, desperation, and anticipation. *\"Works\"* refers to the equipment used to inject heroin, while *\"cooked up\"* describes preparing the drug for injection.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 201, 44, 'It never occurred to him to wonder how much this stuff was cut.', 'Street heroin is often diluted with other substances. Richard is so eager to use the drug that he never considers its purity.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 202, 44, 'On the street the heaviest hit Richie had ever taken was 12 percent pure, and that had put him into a sleep so deep it was nearly a coma.', 'The strongest heroin he had ever previously used was relatively weak compared to what he is about to inject. Even that amount nearly overwhelmed him.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 203, 44, 'He hadn’t even nodded.', '\"Nodding\" refers to the drowsy state heroin users often enter before sleep. Richard skipped even that stage.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 204, 44, 'Just bang and off he went, outta the blue and into the black.', 'The heroin affected him almost instantly, sending him into unconsciousness. The vivid language captures the sudden transition from awareness to oblivion.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 205, 45, 'He injected himself above the elbow and pushed the plunger of his spike home.', 'Richard administers the drug intravenously. The action is described clinically and directly, emphasizing the finality of the moment.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 206, 45, 'The stuff was almost 96 percent pure.', 'The heroin is extraordinarily pure—many times stronger than anything Richard has ever experienced. This sentence explains why his decision is fatal.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 207, 45, 'It hit his bloodstream like a highballing freight and Richie fell down on the bags of heroin, flouring the front of his shirt with it.', 'The comparison to a speeding freight train conveys overwhelming force. The drug enters his system almost explosively. As he collapses, heroin powder scatters across his shirt like flour.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
INSERT INTO `sentences` VALUES ('chapter-1', 208, 45, 'He was dead six minutes later. No great loss.', 'Richard survives the superflu only to die from the addiction that defined his life before the epidemic. His death perfectly illustrates the theme of the second epidemic: people who escaped the disease are ultimately destroyed by their own weaknesses, circumstances, or the collapse of the world around them.', '2026-07-19 15:51:10', '2026-07-19 15:51:10');
